{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Vcw7SS1EJPF5ms3k7xwDaj","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation: phase 6, the continuation format and the row carrier\n2\t\n3\tStatus: **Companion design, phase 6 of `yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md`\n4\t§10.** Written 2026-10-11 (Architect: claude-fable-5-1) from the frozen\n5\tdesign as amended (`8f0b9e38`), the landed 4a evaluator\n6\t(`src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic_register.cljc`) and the 4b stage-1 evaluator\n7\ton branch `srvm-phase4b` (read only), the merged phase-5 derivations\n8\tdesign, the UCF document and its version-2 amendment, the row-carrier\n9\tdraft (`yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md`, body version 3, never landed),\n10\tthe two de Bruijn kernels, and the landed UCF code and harness\n11\t(`src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf.cljc`, `src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/handoff.cljc`,\n12\t`test/yin/vm/ucf/safepoint_harness_test.cljc`). Revision 2 (2026-10-11)\n13\tapplies the codex review\n14\t`collab/1791760000000-architect-srvm-phase6-design-review.gpt-6.1-sol.findings.md`\n15\t(CHANGES_REQUESTED): the task's free environment is carried explicitly\n16\t(§4.4, §6.3), the stack kernel's K slices and tail completion are\n17\tcorrected and gated (§4.3, §8.3), register return destinations are\n18\trecovered from A (§4.2), `act` and `tail` have separate algorithms, the\n19\tvalidator has a complete pure input contract and the carrier's order\n20\t(§3), the static laws use actual-successor live-out (§5.6), blinding is\n21\ta specified re-emission (§5.5), the harness matrix is expanded (§5.2),\n22\t6a is the independent codec (§8.1), and the amendment inventory is\n23\texhaustive (§10). Revision 3 (2026-10-11) applies the codex round-2\n24\treview\n25\t`collab/1791800000000-architect-srvm-phase6-design-review-r2.gpt-6.1-sol.findings.md`\n26\t(CHANGES_REQUESTED): stack lowering bases are cumulative through each\n27\tslice (§4.3), the live operand subtracts the virtual destination before\n28\tmapping (§4.2, §5.6), the free environment's source on lift is specified\n29\twith its owner (§6.3), E2 requires lexical presence and X1 validates the\n30\troot's free environment (§3.2), the harness oracles of rows 15, 20, 22\n31\tand 23 and the segment-wrapper results are corrected (§5.2), the\n32\tcross-lane re-emission takes an explicit stream correspondence (§5.5),\n33\tand the amendment residue is closed (§10.3 R9, U7). **Revision 4\n34\t(2026-10-13, Architect: claude-fable-5-1)** amends the text after slice\n35\t6b merged (`1db08f7d`: `c3d37586` plus the fixes `a396f996`, `f650e046`,\n36\t`bafdec74`), so that §§2.5-2.6, 5.2, 6.1, 6.3, 7, 8.2 state what\n37\t`src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc` (`lift-task`, `lower-task`,\n38\t`check-stores!`, `check-pendings!`, `check-dependencies!`,\n39\t`check-custody!`, `discharge!`, `live-pcs`) does; every amended clause\n40\tis marked \"**Amended after 6b**\" with what changed and why, §10.6\n41\tinventories them, and §11 lists the design choices the code made that\n42\tthe owner has not ruled on. Sources: the engineer report\n43\t`collab/1792270000000-engineer-6b-task-transport.report.md` (design bugs\n44\tB1-B4, deviations 1-10) and the three codex reviews\n45\t(`collab/1792280000000-…`, `1792300000000-…`, `1792320000000-…`). The\n46\tfrozen document is not changed by this one. **Revision 5 (2026-10-13,\n47\tArchitect: claude-fable-5-1)** amends the text after slice 6c\n48\t(branch `srvm-phase6c`: `47ddb1d9` plus the fix round `dc545aaa`,\n49\t`30730c51`; not yet merged at the time of writing), so that §§4.1-4.3,\n50\t5.2, 5.3, 5.5, 6.1, 6.3, 7, 8.3, 9 state what\n51\t`src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic_register/layout.cljc` (`segment`, `space`,\n52\t`phys`, `virt`, `lift-state`, `lower-state`, `canonical-task`,\n53\t`kernel-task`, `lower-defect`, `lift-task`, `lower-task`) and the 6c\n54\ttests do; every amended clause is marked \"**Amended after 6c\n55\t(2026-10-13)**\" with what changed and why, §10.7 inventories them, and\n56\t§11 gains the three questions slice 6c left for the owner. Sources: the\n57\tengineer report `collab/1792340000000-engineer-6c-layouts.report.md`\n58\t(deviations 1-8, design defects D1-D5), the codex review\n59\t`collab/1792350000000-review-6c-layouts.gpt-6.1-sol.findings.md` (F1-F6,\n60\tD1-D5) and the Architect's rulings\n61\t`collab/1792360000000-architect-6c-rulings.report.md` (R1-R6), whose\n62\twording is applied verbatim where it says so.\n63\tSubordinate to [`datom.world.md`](./datom.world.md), including its\n64\tunitarity invariant, and to\n65\t[`yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md`](./yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md)\n66\t(\"the frozen design\"); format and rigor model:\n67\t[`yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.evaluator.md`](./yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.evaluator.md)\n68\tand [`yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.derivations.md`](./yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.derivations.md).\n69\t\n70\tEvery section marks its content **DECIDED** (an owner ruling, frozen\n71\ttext, or code that exists) or **PROPOSED** (a design choice of this\n72\tdocument, open to the reviewer). File references are to the worktree at\n73\t`8f0b9e38`; line numbers are those of that commit; the 4b branch is\n74\tcited as `srvm-phase4b:semantic_register.cljc`, with the line numbers of\n75\tits stage-1 commit (`0f4522b9`) unless a citation says stage 2\n76\t(`bdf48cf4`, committed after revision 2; stage 2 moved the reified\n77\tpayload to `:256`, `create-vm` to `:349-375` and `gc-roots`/`gc-children`\n78\tto `:485-488`, and changed none of the shapes this document reads).\n79\t\n80\tContents: §0 rulings and the one-paragraph answer · §1 the canonical\n81\tframe · §2 the row carrier · §3 the frame validator · §4 layouts · §5\n82\tthe safepoint harness · §6 code and task context in the carrier · §7\n83\tlift and lower · §8 slices, gates and phase 7's entry conditions · §9\n84\tverification honesty · §10 findings and amendments · §11 owner\n85\tquestions · §12 portability.\n86\t\n87\t---\n88\t\n89\t## 0. Rulings and the one-paragraph answer\n90\t\n91\t### 0.1 Rulings that bind this design (DECIDED)\n92\t\n93\t1. **A is the only code identity**; new identities digest under Jing's\n94\t   default (BLAKE3), never SHA-256 (`ucf/code-address` is\n95\t   `jing/segment-key`, `ucf.cljc:247-251`).\n96\t2. **No legacy**: one body version, no reader for older bodies, no\n97\t   compat shim, no migration path; clean breaks.\n98\t3. **Unitarity**: the AST is never lost and is always retrievable\n99\t   wherever code is lowered; no design assumes a tree-less receiver; the\n100\t   segment-to-tree association of the phase-5 design (§9.2 there) is a\n101\t   given, including its completeness rule: an absent entry **or an empty\n102\t   tree set** is incomplete.\n103\t4. **The vector-to-datoms mapping is retired**; the carrier carries\n104\t   positional tuples and rows, never datoms-from-vector.\n105\t5. **dao.stream is the complexity boundary**: no transport mechanics.\n106\t6. **One truth, many interpretations**: the register machine's\n107\t   configuration `C = ⟨seg, pc, W⟩` with `E`, `K` is the canonical frame\n108\t   shape; the stack and register kernels reconstruct it through their\n109\t   layouts (frozen §4.3, §10 phase 6).\n110\t7. **No file of phase 4b or phase 5 is touched**, so this phase runs\n111\t   concurrently with them (§8.5 names the dependencies that remain, and\n112\t   the one old-kernel file 6c must change).\n113\t\n114\t### 0.2 The answer\n115\t\n116\tA continuation is a value: one **canonical frame** of the register\n117\tmachine, `act` or `tail`, with its saved window, its `K` of `:return`\n118\tframes, its environment, its delivery record and its pending wait\n119\t(frozen §2.4, §4.2), plus the task context it needs: the task's **free\n120\tenvironment**, store slice, module stores, parked table, cursor cells, code by"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"47508f4a-f118-4fad-b5f9-49922c52f330","uuid":"03d0aab2-e341-4bac-919d-5aaefee8d595","timestamp":"2026-10-13T08:29:39.216Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-docs-6c/docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md","content":"# yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation: phase 6, the continuation format and the row carrier\n\nStatus: **Companion design, phase 6 of `yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md`\n§10.** Written 2026-10-11 (Architect: claude-fable-5-1) from the frozen\ndesign as amended (`8f0b9e38`), the landed 4a evaluator\n(`src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic_register.cljc`) and the 4b stage-1 evaluator\non branch `srvm-phase4b` (read only), the merged phase-5 derivations\ndesign, the UCF document and its version-2 amendment, the row-carrier\ndraft (`yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md`, body version 3, never landed),\nthe two de Bruijn kernels, and the landed UCF code and harness\n(`src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf.cljc`, `src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/handoff.cljc`,\n`test/yin/vm/ucf/safepoint_harness_test.cljc`). Revision 2 (2026-10-11)\napplies the codex review\n`collab/1791760000000-architect-srvm-phase6-design-review.gpt-6.1-sol.findings.md`\n(CHANGES_REQUESTED): the task's free environment is carried explicitly\n(§4.4, §6.3), the stack kernel's K slices and tail completion are\ncorrected and gated (§4.3, §8.3), register return destinations are\nrecovered from A (§4.2), `act` and `tail` have separate algorithms, the\nvalidator has a complete pure input contract and the carrier's order\n(§3), the static laws use actual-successor live-out (§5.6), blinding is\na specified re-emission (§5.5), the harness matrix is expanded (§5.2),\n6a is the independent codec (§8.1), and the amendment inventory is\nexhaustive (§10). Revision 3 (2026-10-11) applies the codex round-2\nreview\n`collab/1791800000000-architect-srvm-phase6-design-review-r2.gpt-6.1-sol.findings.md`\n(CHANGES_REQUESTED): stack lowering bases are cumulative through each\nslice (§4.3), the live operand subtracts the virtual destination before\nmapping (§4.2, §5.6), the free environment's source on lift is specified\nwith its owner (§6.3), E2 requires lexical presence and X1 validates the\nroot's free environment (§3.2), the harness oracles of rows 15, 20, 22\nand 23 and the segment-wrapper results are corrected (§5.2), the\ncross-lane re-emission takes an explicit stream correspondence (§5.5),\nand the amendment residue is closed (§10.3 R9, U7). **Revision 4\n(2026-10-13, Architect: claude-fable-5-1)** amends the text after slice\n6b merged (`1db08f7d`: `c3d37586` plus the fixes `a396f996`, `f650e046`,\n`bafdec74`), so that §§2.5-2.6, 5.2, 6.1, 6.3, 7, 8.2 state what\n`src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc` (`lift-task`, `lower-task`,\n`check-stores!`, `check-pendings!`, `check-dependencies!`,\n`check-custody!`, `discharge!`, `live-pcs`) does; every amended clause\nis marked \"**Amended after 6b**\" with what changed and why, §10.6\ninventories them, and §11 lists the design choices the code made that\nthe owner has not ruled on. Sources: the engineer report\n`collab/1792270000000-engineer-6b-task-transport.report.md` (design bugs\nB1-B4, deviations 1-10) and the three codex reviews\n(`collab/1792280000000-…`, `1792300000000-…`, `1792320000000-…`). The\nfrozen document is not changed by this one. **Revision 5 (2026-10-13,\nArchitect: claude-fable-5-1)** amends the text after slice 6c\n(branch `srvm-phase6c`: `47ddb1d9` plus the fix round `dc545aaa`,\n`30730c51`; not yet merged at the time of writing), so that §§4.1-4.3,\n5.2, 5.3, 5.5, 6.1, 6.3, 7, 8.3, 9 state what\n`src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic_register/layout.cljc` (`segment`, `space`,\n`phys`, `virt`, `lift-state`, `lower-state`, `canonical-task`,\n`kernel-task`, `lower-defect`, `lift-task`, `lower-task`) and the 6c\ntests do; every amended clause is marked \"**Amended after 6c\n(2026-10-13)**\" with what changed and why, §10.7 inventories them, and\n§11 gains the three questions slice 6c left for the owner. Sources: the\nengineer report `collab/1792340000000-engineer-6c-layouts.report.md`\n(deviations 1-8, design defects D1-D5), the codex review\n`collab/1792350000000-review-6c-layouts.gpt-6.1-sol.findings.md` (F1-F6,\nD1-D5) and the Architect's rulings\n`collab/1792360000000-architect-6c-rulings.report.md` (R1-R6), whose\nwording is applied verbatim where it says so.\nSubordinate to [`datom.world.md`](./datom.world.md), including its\nunitarity invariant, and to\n[`yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md`](./yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md)\n(\"the frozen design\"); format and rigor model:\n[`yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.evaluator.md`](./yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.evaluator.md)\nand [`yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.derivations.md`](./yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.derivations.md).\n\nEvery section marks its content **DECIDED** (an owner ruling, frozen\ntext, or code that exists) or **PROPOSED** (a design choice of this\ndocument, open to the reviewer). File references are to the worktree at\n`8f0b9e38`; line numbers are those of that commit; the 4b branch is\ncited as `srvm-phase4b:semantic_register.cljc`, with the line numbers of\nits stage-1 commit (`0f4522b9`) unless a citation says stage 2\n(`bdf48cf4`, committed after revision 2; stage 2 moved the reified\npayload to `:256`, `create-vm` to `:349-375` and `gc-roots`/`gc-children`\nto `:485-488`, and changed none of the shapes this document reads).\n\nContents: §0 rulings and the one-paragraph answer · §1 the canonical\nframe · §2 the row carrier · §3 the frame validator · §4 layouts · §5\nthe safepoint harness · §6 code and task context in the carrier · §7\nlift and lower · §8 slices, gates and phase 7's entry conditions · §9\nverification honesty · §10 findings and amendments · §11 owner\nquestions · §12 portability.\n\n---\n\n## 0. Rulings and the one-paragraph answer\n\n### 0.1 Rulings that bind this design (DECIDED)\n\n1. **A is the only code identity**; new identities digest under Jing's\n   default (BLAKE3), never SHA-256 (`ucf/code-address` is\n   `jing/segment-key`, `ucf.cljc:247-251`).\n2. **No legacy**: one body version, no reader for older bodies, no\n   compat shim, no migration path; clean breaks.\n3. **Unitarity**: the AST is never lost and is always retrievable\n   wherever code is lowered; no design assumes a tree-less receiver; the\n   segment-to-tree association of the phase-5 design (§9.2 there) is a\n   given, including its completeness rule: an absent entry **or an empty\n   tree set** is incomplete.\n4. **The vector-to-datoms mapping is retired**; the carrier carries\n   positional tuples and rows, never datoms-from-vector.\n5. **dao.stream is the complexity boundary**: no transport mechanics.\n6. **One truth, many interpretations**: the register machine's\n   configuration `C = ⟨seg, pc, W⟩` with `E`, `K` is the canonical frame\n   shape; the stack and register kernels reconstruct it through their\n   layouts (frozen §4.3, §10 phase 6).\n7. **No file of phase 4b or phase 5 is touched**, so this phase runs\n   concurrently with them (§8.5 names the dependencies that remain, and\n   the one old-kernel file 6c must change).\n\n### 0.2 The answer\n\nA continuation is a value: one **canonical frame** of the register\nmachine, `act` or `tail`, with its saved window, its `K` of `:return`\nframes, its environment, its delivery record and its pending wait\n(frozen §2.4, §4.2), plus the task context it needs: the task's **free\nenvironment**, store slice, module stores, parked table, cursor cells, code by","numLines":120,"startLine":1,"totalLines":2233}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Vcw7SS1EJPF5ms3k7xwDaj","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
