{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HDV7awycPx6oqhfYAcdYGj","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t781a9ba8 Merge branch 'srvm-phase6c': slice 6c, the register and stack layouts and the cross-engine lanes of the safepoint harness\n2\t30730c51 test(yin.vm.semantic-register): scoped native layout worlds, guarded law-4 controls, nested free-environment refusals, receiver image functions pinned (phase 6c review)\n3\tdc545aaa fix(yin.vm.semantic-register): layout refusals for ambiguous images and free-environment procedures, law-4 controls, an ambiguous virt refusal, audit allowlist (phase 6c review)\n4\t(ns yin.vm.semantic-register.layout\n5\t  \"Phase 6c (docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md §4):\n6\t   the de Bruijn register and stack kernels reconstruct the canonical\n7\t   frame of the register machine through their layouts, and lower it\n8\t   back.\n9\t\n10\t   Static half, per segment A: `segment` derives R(A) and H(A) and reads\n11\t   off the register pairing (`phys`, the restricted inverse `virt`, the\n12\t   kernel's `live` as live-out with tail boundaries `[]`), the stack\n13\t   correspondence (`h->a`, `a->h`, every `:push` removed) and the operand\n14\t   layout `stack-layout` (the values pushed and not yet consumed while\n15\t   control is inside a pc's expression). A `space` indexes segments by\n16\t   the kernels' image identities, R and H, which are checksums: A is the\n17\t   only code identity.\n18\t\n19\t   Dynamic half: `lift-state` reads a kernel's wait entry, parked record\n20\t   or reified payload as the canonical `act` or `tail` payload the\n21\t   semantic-register evaluator mints (`{:segment A :pc :env :window :k\n22\t   :deliver}`, `{:segment A :site :k :deliver}`, engine fields carried);\n23\t   `lower-state` is its inverse. The register kernel's return\n24\t   destinations are recovered from A, never from the physical `:dest`;\n25\t   the stack kernel's operand stack is sliced `[previous-base, base)` per\n26\t   frame and lowered with cumulative bases. `E` is the free environment\n27\t   merged under the chain's positional frames (§4.4); the inverse reads\n28\t   each frame back from `E` by the chain, never the free environment.\n29\t\n30\t   Task level: `canonical-task` presents a quiescent kernel as a\n31\t   semantic-register machine for `yin.vm.ucf.rows/lift-task`;\n32\t   `kernel-task` restores a machine `rows/lower-task` produced into a\n33\t   fresh kernel; `lift-task` and `lower-task` compose them with the row\n34\t   carrier, the lower refusing what a kernel cannot hold before any\n35\t   stream is attached. A layout never runs code, never fills a binding\n36\t   from the receiver and never invents a safepoint (§4.5).\"\n37\t  (:require [dao.jing :as jing]\n38\t            [yin.vm.debruijn-code :as dcode]\n39\t            [yin.vm.debruijn-register-code :as rcode]\n40\t            [yin.vm.debruijn.register :as register]\n41\t            [yin.vm.debruijn.stack :as stack]\n42\t            [yin.vm :as vm]\n43\t            [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\n44\t            [yin.vm.module :as module]\n45\t            [yin.vm.semantic-register.analysis :as analysis]\n46\t            [yin.vm.semantic-register.code :as code]\n47\t            [yin.vm.semantic-register.derive :as derive]\n48\t            [yin.vm.ucf.rows :as rows]\n49\t            [yin.vm.values :as values]))\n50\t\n51\t\n52\t(defn- refuse!\n53\t  [status kind data]\n54\t  (throw (ex-info \"Layout refused\" (merge data (assoc {} :yin.k/status status :yin.k/kind kind)))))\n55\t\n56\t\n57\t;; =============================================================================\n58\t;; Static half: one segment\n59\t;; =============================================================================\n60\t\n61\t(defn- operands\n62\t  \"The register operands of an A tuple, destination first, then its uses\n63\t   in table order.\"\n64\t  [t]\n65\t  (into (if-some [r (code/rd t)] [r] []) (code/uses t)))\n66\t\n67\t\n68\t(defn- register-operands\n69\t  \"The `:reg`/`:regs` operands of an R tuple in table order (the `:live`\n70\t   slot is `:data`, never paired).\"\n71\t  [t]\n72\t  (into []\n73\t        (mapcat (fn [[[_ kind] x]] (case kind :reg [x] :regs x [])))\n74\t        (map vector (get rcode/opcode-table (nth t 0)) (rest t))))\n75\t\n76\t\n77\t(defn register-pairs\n78\t  \"`[pc virtual physical]` for every register operand of every pc: A's\n79\t   tuple and R's name their registers in the same slots (phase-5 §2.4).\"\n80\t  [v image]\n81\t  (into []\n82\t        (mapcat (fn [pc]\n83\t                  (map (fn [x s] [pc x s])\n84\t                       (operands (nth v pc))\n85\t                       (register-operands (nth (:instructions image) pc)))))\n86\t        (range (count v))))\n87\t\n88\t\n89\t(defn- phys-maps\n90\t  \"Per body, `{virtual physical}` read off the pairs; the first pc that\n91\t   names a virtual wins (register-pairing checks they agree).\"\n92\t  [bodies pairs]\n93\t  (reduce (fn [acc [pc x s]]\n94\t            (let [b (code/body-index bodies pc)]\n95\t              (if (contains? (nth acc b) x) acc (assoc-in acc [b x] s))))\n96\t          (vec (repeat (count bodies) {}))\n97\t          pairs))\n98\t\n99\t\n100\t(defn correspondence\n101\t  \"§4.3 static item 1: H with every `:push` removed corresponds one to one,\n102\t   in order, with A. Answers `{:a->h [h-pc …] :h->a {h-pc a-pc}}`.\"\n103\t  [h]\n104\t  (reduce (fn [acc hpc]\n105\t            (if (= :push (nth (nth h hpc) 0))\n106\t              acc\n107\t              (-> acc\n108\t                  (update :a->h conj hpc)\n109\t                  (assoc-in [:h->a hpc] (count (:a->h acc))))))\n110\t          {:a->h [] :h->a {}}\n111\t          (range (count h))))\n112\t\n113\t\n114\t(def ^:private pushing-ops\n115\t  \"The parse nodes whose children before the current one are pushed:\n116\t   `:call` (the operator and earlier operands), `:ffi-call` (earlier\n117\t   operands) and `:stream-put` (the target, while the value runs).\"\n118\t  #{:call :ffi-call :stream-put})\n119\t\n120\t\n121\t(defn- stack-layouts\n122\t  \"§4.3 static item 2 for every pc of every body: `{pc [virtual …]}`,\n123\t   bottom to top, over the parse tree's ancestors outermost first.\"\n124\t  [v bodies]\n125\t  (letfn [(walk\n126\t            [out node pending]\n127\t            (let [out (assoc out (:pc node) pending)\n128\t                  pushes? (contains? pushing-ops (:op node))\n129\t                  uses (when pushes? (code/uses (nth v (:pc node))))]\n130\t              (reduce (fn [out [i child]]\n131\t                        (walk out child (if pushes? (into pending (take i uses)) pending)))\n132\t                      out\n133\t                      (map-indexed vector (:children node)))))]\n134\t    (reduce (fn [out body] (walk out (:expr body) [])) {} bodies)))\n135\t\n136\t\n137\t(defn segment\n138\t  \"The static facts of one admitted A vector `v`, for both kernels.\"\n139\t  [v]\n140\t  (let [bodies (code/parse v)\n141\t        r (derive/register-image v)\n142\t        h (:image (derive/stack-image v))\n143\t        pairs (register-pairs v r)]\n144\t    (merge {:vector v\n145\t            :address (jing/segment-key v)\n146\t            :bodies bodies\n147\t            :analysis (analysis/analyze v)\n148\t            :register r\n149\t            :register-id (rcode/register-hash r)\n150\t            :stack h\n151\t            :stack-id (dcode/image-hash h)\n152\t            :pairs pairs\n153\t            :phys (phys-maps bodies pairs)\n154\t            :layouts (stack-layouts v bodies)}\n155\t           (correspondence h))))\n156\t\n157\t\n158\t(defn space\n159\t  \"Segments by A, and A by each kernel's image identity. `segments` is a\n160\t   seq of `segment` results or of A vectors.\"\n161\t  [segments]\n162\t  (reduce (fn [acc s]\n163\t            (let [s (if (map? s) s (segment s))\n164\t                  a (:address s)]\n165\t              (-> acc\n166\t                  (assoc-in [:segments a] s)\n167\t                  (update-in [:register (:register-id s)] (fnil conj #{}) a)\n168\t                  (update-in [:stack (:stack-id s)] (fnil conj #{}) a))))\n169\t          {:segments {} :register {} :stack {}}\n170\t          segments))\n171\t\n172\t\n173\t(defn segment-of\n174\t  \"The segment A names in `space`.\"\n175\t  [space a]\n176\t  (or (get-in space [:segments a])\n177\t      (refuse! :yin.k/unsatisfied :segment {:yin.k/segment a})))\n178\t\n179\t\n180\t(defn- image-segment\n181\t  \"The segment whose `kind` image is `ident`: an identity is a checksum,\n182\t   so two A deriving one image are ambiguous and refused.\"\n183\t  [space kind ident]\n184\t  (let [as (get-in space [kind ident])]\n185\t    (cond\n186\t      (empty? as) (refuse! :yin.k/non-portable :unknown-image {:yin.k/image ident})\n187\t      (< 1 (count as)) (refuse! :yin.k/non-portable :ambiguous-image {:yin.k/image ident})\n188\t      :else (segment-of space (first as)))))\n189\t\n190\t\n191\t(defn- inst\n192\t  [seg pc]\n193\t  (nth (:vector seg) pc))\n194\t\n195\t\n196\t(defn- body-of\n197\t  [seg pc]\n198\t  (code/body-index (:bodies seg) pc))\n199\t\n200\t\n201\t(defn phys\n202\t  \"`phys(body(pc), x)`: the physical register R names for virtual `x` in\n203\t   the body holding `pc`.\"\n204\t  [seg pc x]\n205\t  (let [s (get (nth (:phys seg) (body-of seg pc)) x)]\n206\t    (when (nil? s) (refuse! :yin.k/non-portable :register-layout {:yin.k/pc pc :yin.k/register x}))\n207\t    s))\n208\t\n209\t\n210\t(defn live-out\n211\t  \"`live-out*(p)`: the union of `L(q)` over p's actual successors (empty\n212\t   for a tail call).\"\n213\t  [seg p]\n214\t  (reduce (fn [acc q] (into acc (analysis/live (:analysis seg) q)))\n215\t          #{}\n216\t          (analysis/successors (:vector seg) p)))\n217\t\n218\t\n219\t(defn register-live\n220\t  \"§5.6 item 3: the `live` operand R must carry at boundary `p`,\n221\t   `(sort (map phys (disj live-out*(p) rd)))`, the destination removed as\n222\t   a virtual id before mapping; `[]` at a tail call.\"\n223\t  [seg p]\n224\t  (vec (sort (map #(phys seg p %) (disj (live-out seg p) (code/rd (inst seg p)))))))\n225\t\n226\t\n227\t(defn virt\n228\t  \"The restricted inverse of `phys` at boundary `p`: the virtual of\n229\t   `live-out*(p)` held in physical `s`. A slot outside that image (only a\n230\t   tampered entry names one) reads as the one virtual of the body R maps\n231\t   there, so the frame validator judges the window; an ambiguous slot is\n232\t   refused.\"\n233\t  [seg p s]\n234\t  (let [m (nth (:phys seg) (body-of seg p))\n235\t        live (filterv #(= s (get m %)) (sort (live-out seg p)))\n236\t        named (filterv #(= s (get m %)) (sort (keys m)))]\n237\t    (cond\n238\t      (= 1 (count live)) (first live)\n239\t      (and (empty? live) (= 1 (count named))) (first named)\n240\t      :else (refuse! :yin.k/non-portable :register-layout {:yin.k/pc p :yin.k/register s}))))\n241\t\n242\t\n243\t(defn stack-layout\n244\t  \"§4.3: the virtual registers pushed and not yet consumed while control\n245\t   is inside the expression at A pc `p`, bottom to top.\"\n246\t  [seg p]\n247\t  (get (:layouts seg) p))\n248\t\n249\t\n250\t(defn chain\n251\t  \"The closure pcs owning the body that holds `pc`, outermost first.\"\n252\t  [seg pc]\n253\t  (loop [b (body-of seg pc) out ()]\n254\t    (if-let [owner (:owner (nth (:bodies seg) b))]\n255\t      (recur (body-of seg owner) (conj out owner))\n256\t      (vec out))))\n257\t\n258\t\n259\t(defn- params\n260\t  [seg c]\n261\t  (nth (inst seg c) 2))\n262\t\n263\t\n264\t(defn env-of\n265\t  \"§4.4 forward: `E` at `pc` from the positional frames `F` (outermost\n266\t   first, values already canonical), the task's free environment and the\n267\t   activation's module store.\"\n268\t  [seg pc free-env frames store-of]\n269\t  (let [cs (chain seg pc)]\n270\t    (when-not (= (count cs) (count frames))\n271\t      (refuse! :yin.k/non-portable :frame-depth {:yin.k/pc pc :yin.k/depth (count frames)}))\n272\t    (cond-> (reduce (fn [e [c f]] (merge e (engine/bind-params (params seg c) f)))\n273\t                    (or free-env {})\n274\t                    (map vector cs frames))\n275\t      (some? store-of) (assoc engine/store-of-key store-of))))\n276\t\n277\t\n278\t(defn frames-of\n279\t  \"§4.4 inverse: `F[i] = (mapv #(get E %) params(cᵢ))` over the chain at\n280\t   `pc`. An outer value a shadowing inner binder hides reads as the inner\n281\t   one; the canonical frame never held it.\"\n282\t  [seg pc env]\n283\t  (mapv (fn [c] (mapv #(get env %) (params seg c))) (chain seg pc)))\n284\t\n285\t\n286\t;; =============================================================================\n287\t;; Kernel dispatch\n288\t;; =============================================================================\n289\t\n290\t(defn kernel-kind\n291\t  \"`:stack` or `:register`, by the kernel's link format.\"\n292\t  [k]\n293\t  (let [f (when (satisfies? module/IModuleKernel k) (:format (module/link-format k)))]\n294\t    (cond\n295\t      (= stack/format-tag f) :stack\n296\t      (= register/format-tag f) :register\n297\t      :else (refuse! :yin.k/unsupported :kernel {:yin.k/format f}))))\n298\t\n299\t\n300\t(defn- image-pc\n301\t  \"`[segment rel-pc]` of absolute kernel pc `pc`.\"\n302\t  [kind k space pc]\n303\t  (let [[ident rel] (or (if (= :stack kind) (stack/image-pc k pc) (register/image-pc k pc))\n304\t                        (refuse! :yin.k/non-portable :unknown-image {:yin.k/pc pc}))]\n305\t    [(image-segment space kind ident) rel]))\n306\t\n307\t\n308\t(defn offset\n309\t  \"The offset of segment `seg`'s image in kernel `k`'s code space.\"\n310\t  [kind k seg]\n311\t  (let [ident (if (= :stack kind) (:stack-id seg) (:register-id seg))]\n312\t    (or (if (= :stack kind) (stack/absolute-pc k [ident 0]) (register/absolute-pc k [ident 0]))\n313\t        (refuse! :yin.k/unsatisfied :image-not-attached {:yin.k/segment (:address seg)}))))\n314\t\n315\t\n316\t(def ^:private parking-ops\n317\t  \"A1: the instructions a resume pc may follow, besides a non-tail call.\"\n318\t  #{:stream-next :stream-put :ffi-call :park :current-continuation})\n319\t\n320\t\n321\t(defn- safepoint!\n322\t  \"Refuse `:yin.k/not-at-safepoint` unless the A instruction before `pc`\n323\t   parks (a tail call for a tail state): a layout never invents a\n324\t   safepoint (§4.5).\"\n325\t  [seg pc tail?]\n326\t  (let [t (when (and (integer? pc) (< 0 pc) (<= pc (count (:vector seg)))) (inst seg (dec pc)))\n327\t        op (when t (nth t 0))]\n328\t    (when-not (and t\n329\t                   (= (body-of seg (dec pc)) (body-of seg (min pc (dec (count (:vector seg))))))\n330\t                   (if tail?\n331\t                     (code/tail-call? t)\n332\t                     (or (contains? parking-ops op) (and (= :call op) (not (code/tail-call? t))))))\n333\t      (refuse! :yin.k/not-at-safepoint nil {:yin.k/pc pc}))))\n334\t\n335\t\n336\t(defn- h->a\n337\t  \"The A pc of H pc `hpc`; a `:push` has none and is no safepoint.\"\n338\t  [seg hpc]\n339\t  (or (get (:h->a seg) hpc) (refuse! :yin.k/not-at-safepoint nil {:yin.k/pc hpc})))\n340\t\n341\t\n342\t(defn- a->h\n343\t  [seg pc]\n344\t  (nth (:a->h seg) pc))\n345\t\n346\t\n347\t;; =============================================================================\n348\t;; Values: positional closures and kernel continuations, both ways\n349\t;; =============================================================================\n350\t;;\n351\t;; A lift context `cx` is {:kind :kernel :space :free-env :owner}; a lower\n352\t;; context `lx` adds :address, naming a canonical payload's or closure's\n353\t;; :segment as A.\n354\t\n355\t(declare lift-state lower-state canonical-value positional-value)\n356\t\n357\t\n358\t(defn- walk-value\n359\t  \"`x` with its guest collections rebuilt around `f`, which converts\n360\t   closures and continuations.\"\n361\t  [f x]\n362\t  (cond\n363\t    (values/host-typed? x) (f x)\n364\t    (map? x) (into {} (map (fn [[k v]] [(walk-value f k) (walk-value f v)])) x)\n365\t    (vector? x) (mapv #(walk-value f %) x)\n366\t    (set? x) (into #{} (map #(walk-value f %)) x)\n367\t    (seq? x) (apply list (map #(walk-value f %) x))\n368\t    :else x))\n369\t\n370\t\n371\t(defn- canonical-closure\n372\t  \"§4.4: a positional closure as the canonical `{:type :closure :params\n373\t   :entry :segment :env}`: `params` from A's `:closure` at the owner of\n374\t   the entry body, `env` by the forward rule over the closure's frames.\"\n375\t  [cx c]\n376\t  (let [[seg rel] (image-pc (:kind cx) (:kernel cx) (:space cx) (:body-pc c))\n377\t        entry (if (= :stack (:kind cx)) (h->a seg rel) rel)\n378\t        owner (:owner (nth (:bodies seg) (body-of seg entry)))\n379\t        _ (when-not (and owner (= entry (nth (inst seg owner) 3)))\n380\t            (refuse! :yin.k/non-portable :closure-origin {:yin.k/entry entry}))\n381\t        ps (params seg owner)]\n382\t    (when-not (= (count ps) (:arity c))\n383\t      (refuse! :yin.k/non-portable :closure-binders {:yin.k/entry entry}))\n384\t    {:type :closure :params ps :entry entry :segment (:address seg)\n385\t     :env (env-of seg owner (:free-env cx)\n386\t                  (mapv (fn [f] (mapv #(canonical-value cx %) f)) (:frames c))\n387\t                  (:store-of c))}))\n388\t\n389\t\n390\t(defn- canonical-value*\n391\t  [cx x]\n392\t  (cond\n393\t    (values/closure? x) (values/closure (:owner cx) (canonical-closure cx (values/payload x)))\n394\t    (values/continuation? x)\n395\t    (values/continuation (:owner cx) (assoc (lift-state cx (values/payload x)) :type :reified-continuation))\n396\t    :else x))\n397\t\n398\t\n399\t(defn canonical-value\n400\t  \"Kernel value `x` with every positional closure and kernel continuation\n401\t   reconstructed canonically (cx: a lift context).\"\n402\t  [cx x]\n403\t  (walk-value #(canonical-value* cx %) x))\n404\t\n405\t\n406\t(defn- address-of\n407\t  [lx seg-id]\n408\t  (let [a ((:address lx) seg-id)]\n409\t    (when (nil? a) (refuse! :yin.k/non-portable :unaddressed-segment {:yin.k/hint seg-id}))\n410\t    a))\n411\t\n412\t\n413\t(defn- positional-closure\n414\t  \"The inverse of canonical-closure: the entry's absolute pc in the\n415\t   receiving kernel, the frames read back from `env` by the owner's chain.\"\n416\t  [lx c]\n417\t  (let [seg (segment-of (:space lx) (address-of lx (:segment c)))\n418\t        entry (:entry c)\n419\t        owner (:owner (nth (:bodies seg) (body-of seg entry)))\n420\t        store-of (engine/env-store-of (:env c))]\n421\t    (when-not (and owner (= entry (nth (inst seg owner) 3)) (= (vec (:params c)) (vec (params seg owner))))\n422\t      (refuse! :yin.k/undecodable :closure-binders {:yin.k/entry entry}))\n423\t    (cond-> {:type :closure :arity (count (:params c))\n424\t             :body-pc (+ (offset (:kind lx) (:kernel lx) seg) (if (= :stack (:kind lx)) (a->h seg entry) entry))\n425\t             :frames (mapv (fn [f] (mapv #(positional-value lx %) f)) (frames-of seg owner (:env c)))}\n426\t      (some? store-of) (assoc :store-of store-of))))\n427\t\n428\t\n429\t(defn- positional-value*\n430\t  [lx x]\n431\t  (cond\n432\t    (values/closure? x) (values/closure (:owner lx) (positional-closure lx (values/payload x)))\n433\t    (values/continuation? x)\n434\t    (values/continuation (:owner lx) (merge {:type :reified-continuation} (lower-state lx (values/payload x))))\n435\t    :else x))\n436\t\n437\t\n438\t(defn positional-value\n439\t  \"Canonical value `x` with every closure and continuation lowered into\n440\t   the receiving kernel (lx: a lower context).\"\n441\t  [lx x]\n442\t  (walk-value #(positional-value* lx %) x))\n443\t\n444\t\n445\t;; =============================================================================\n446\t;; Lift: a kernel payload as the canonical act or tail\n447\t;; =============================================================================\n448\t\n449\t(def ^:private kernel-keys\n450\t  \"The register payload keys of either kernel; every other key of an\n451\t   entry is the engine's and travels in the pending.\"\n452\t  #{:segment :site-pc :pc :frames :regs :live :continuation :dest :resume-mode\n453\t    :format :hash :image :images :store-of :stack})\n454\t\n455\t\n456\t(defn- canonical-env\n457\t  [cx seg pc frames store-of]\n458\t  (env-of seg pc (:free-env cx) (mapv (fn [f] (mapv #(canonical-value cx %) f)) frames) store-of))\n459\t\n460\t\n461\t(defn- register-window\n462\t  \"§4.2 step 4: `{virt(site, s) V}` over the entry's `[s V]` pairs.\"\n463\t  [cx seg site regs]\n464\t  (into {} (map (fn [[s x]] [(virt seg site s) (canonical-value cx x)])) regs))\n465\t\n466\t\n467\t(defn- register-kframe\n468\t  \"§4.2 step 6, one frame independently: its own image row and A, `rd`\n469\t   from A, never the physical `:dest`.\"\n470\t  [cx f]\n471\t  (let [[seg pc] (image-pc :register (:kernel cx) (:space cx) (:return-pc f))]\n472\t    (safepoint! seg pc false)\n473\t    {:type :return :segment (:address seg) :pc pc\n474\t     :env (canonical-env cx seg pc (:frames f) (:store-of f))\n475\t     :window (register-window cx seg (dec pc) (:regs f))\n476\t     :rd (code/rd (inst seg (dec pc)))}))\n477\t\n478\t\n479\t(defn- lift-register\n480\t  [cx entry]\n481\t  (let [[seg pc] (image-pc :register (:kernel cx) (:space cx) (:pc entry))\n482\t        tail? (= :return-result (:resume-mode entry))\n483\t        _ (safepoint! seg pc tail?)\n484\t        k (mapv #(register-kframe cx %) (:continuation entry))]\n485\t    (if tail?\n486\t      {:segment (:address seg) :site (dec pc) :k k :deliver {:deliver :return}}\n487\t      {:segment (:address seg) :pc pc\n488\t       :env (canonical-env cx seg pc (:frames entry) (:store-of entry))\n489\t       :window (register-window cx seg (dec pc) (:regs entry))\n490\t       :k k\n491\t       :deliver {:deliver :rd :rd (code/rd (inst seg (dec pc)))}})))\n492\t\n493\t\n494\t(defn slices\n495\t  \"§4.3's K slices of operand stack `st` under return frames whose bases\n496\t   are `bases`, outermost first: `St[b(i-1), b(i))` per frame with\n497\t   `b(-1) = 0`, then the current activation's `St[b(m-1), n)`.\"\n498\t  [st bases]\n499\t  (let [bounds (into [0] bases)]\n500\t    (conj (mapv (fn [lo hi] (subvec st lo hi)) bounds (rest bounds))\n501\t          (subvec st (peek bounds) (count st)))))\n502\t\n503\t\n504\t(defn- slice-window\n505\t  \"`(zipmap (stack-layout (dec pc)) slice)`; the two have equal length.\"\n506\t  [cx seg pc slice]\n507\t  (let [layout (stack-layout seg (dec pc))]\n508\t    (when-not (= (count layout) (count slice))\n509\t      (refuse! :yin.k/non-portable :stack-layout {:yin.k/pc pc :yin.k/layout layout :yin.k/slice (count slice)}))\n510\t    (zipmap layout (map #(canonical-value cx %) slice))))\n511\t\n512\t\n513\t(defn- stack-site\n514\t  \"`[segment site]`: the A pc of the parking instruction before absolute\n515\t   stack resume pc `abs`.\"\n516\t  [cx abs]\n517\t  (let [[seg rel] (image-pc :stack (:kernel cx) (:space cx) abs)]\n518\t    [seg (h->a seg (dec rel))]))\n519\t\n520\t\n521\t(defn- lift-stack\n522\t  [cx entry]\n523\t  (let [st (vec (:stack entry))\n524\t        frames (vec (:continuation entry))\n525\t        bases (mapv :stack-base frames)\n526\t        _ (when-not (and (every? integer? bases) (apply <= 0 (conj bases (count st))))\n527\t            (refuse! :yin.k/non-portable :stack-base {:yin.k/bases bases}))\n528\t        parts (slices st bases)\n529\t        [seg site] (stack-site cx (:pc entry))\n530\t        tail? (code/tail-call? (inst seg site))\n531\t        _ (safepoint! seg (inc site) tail?)\n532\t        k (mapv (fn [f slice]\n533\t                  (let [[fseg fsite] (stack-site cx (:return-pc f))\n534\t                        pc (inc fsite)]\n535\t                    (safepoint! fseg pc false)\n536\t                    {:type :return :segment (:address fseg) :pc pc\n537\t                     :env (canonical-env cx fseg pc (:frames f) (:store-of f))\n538\t                     :window (slice-window cx fseg pc slice)\n539\t                     :rd (code/rd (inst fseg fsite))}))\n540\t                frames parts)]\n541\t    (if tail?\n542\t      ;; frozen §2.4: the current frames, store-of and slice are dead\n543\t      {:segment (:address seg) :site site :k k :deliver {:deliver :return}}\n544\t      (let [pc (inc site)]\n545\t        {:segment (:address seg) :pc pc\n546\t         :env (canonical-env cx seg pc (:frames entry) (:store-of entry))\n547\t         :window (slice-window cx seg pc (peek parts))\n548\t         :k k\n549\t         :deliver {:deliver :rd :rd (code/rd (inst seg site))}}))))\n550\t\n551\t\n552\t(defn lift-state\n553\t  \"A kernel's wait entry, parked record or reified payload as the\n554\t   canonical act or tail payload (§4.2, §4.3), engine fields carried.\"\n555\t  [cx entry]\n556\t  (let [fields (apply dissoc entry kernel-keys)]\n557\t    (merge (cond-> fields (contains? fields :datom) (update :datom #(canonical-value cx %)))\n558\t           (if (= :stack (:kind cx)) (lift-stack cx entry) (lift-register cx entry)))))\n559\t\n560\t\n561\t(defn lift-context\n562\t  \"The lift context of kernel `k` over `space`; positional closures and\n563\t   kernel continuations are reminted under `owner`.\"\n564\t  [k space owner]\n565\t  (assoc {} :kind (kernel-kind k) :kernel k :space space :free-env (or (:free-env k) {}) :owner owner))\n566\t\n567\t\n568\t;; =============================================================================\n569\t;; Lower: a canonical act or tail into a kernel\n570\t;; =============================================================================\n571\t\n572\t(defn- lower-frames\n573\t  [lx seg pc env]\n574\t  (mapv (fn [f] (mapv #(positional-value lx %) f)) (frames-of seg pc env)))\n575\t\n576\t\n577\t(defn- payload-segment\n578\t  [lx p]\n579\t  (segment-of (:space lx) (address-of lx (:segment p))))\n580\t\n581\t\n582\t(defn- lower-regs\n583\t  \"`(sort-by first [[phys(v) V] …])` over window `w`.\"\n584\t  [lx seg site w]\n585\t  (vec (sort-by first (map (fn [[x v]] [(phys seg site x) (positional-value lx v)]) w))))\n586\t\n587\t\n588\t(defn- register-k\n589\t  [lx k]\n590\t  (mapv (fn [f]\n591\t          (let [seg (payload-segment lx f)\n592\t                off (offset :register (:kernel lx) seg)\n593\t                pc (:pc f)\n594\t                regs (lower-regs lx seg (dec pc) (:window f))\n595\t                store-of (engine/env-store-of (:env f))]\n596\t            (cond-> {:site-pc (+ off pc -1) :return-pc (+ off pc)\n597\t                     :frames (lower-frames lx seg pc (:env f))\n598\t                     :regs regs :live (mapv first regs)\n599\t                     :dest (phys seg (dec pc) (:rd f))}\n600\t              (some? store-of) (assoc :store-of store-of))))\n601\t        k))\n602\t\n603\t\n604\t(defn- lower-register\n605\t  [lx p fill]\n606\t  (let [k (:kernel lx)\n607\t        seg (payload-segment lx p)\n608\t        off (offset :register k seg)\n609\t        common (cond-> {:segment (:segment k) :format register/format-tag :hash (:hash k)\n610\t                        :image (:register-id seg) :continuation (register-k lx (:k p))}\n611\t                 (< 1 (count (:images k))) (assoc :images (:images k)))]\n612\t    (if (contains? p :site)\n613\t      (cond-> (merge common {:site-pc (+ off (:site p)) :pc (+ off (:site p) 1)\n614\t                             :frames (get fill :frames []) :regs [] :live [] :dest nil\n615\t                             :resume-mode :return-result})\n616\t        (some? (:store-of fill)) (assoc :store-of (:store-of fill)))\n617\t      (let [pc (:pc p)\n618\t            regs (lower-regs lx seg (dec pc) (:window p))\n619\t            store-of (engine/env-store-of (:env p))]\n620\t        (cond-> (merge common {:site-pc (+ off pc -1) :pc (+ off pc)\n621\t                               :frames (lower-frames lx seg pc (:env p))\n622\t                               :regs regs :live (mapv first regs)\n623\t                               :dest (phys seg (dec pc) (get-in p [:deliver :rd]))\n624\t                               :resume-mode :write-result})\n625\t          (some? store-of) (assoc :store-of store-of))))))\n626\t\n627\t\n628\t(defn- layout-slice\n629\t  \"`(mapv W (stack-layout (dec pc)))`, every member present in W.\"\n630\t  [lx seg pc w]\n631\t  (mapv (fn [x]\n632\t          (when-not (contains? w x)\n633\t            (refuse! :yin.k/undecodable :window-missing {:yin.k/pc pc :yin.k/register x}))\n634\t          (positional-value lx (get w x)))\n635\t        (stack-layout seg (dec pc))))\n636\t\n637\t\n638\t(defn- stack-k\n639\t  \"`[frames stack]`: each return frame's slice appended in order, its base\n640\t   the cumulative length through its own slice (§4.3), `b(i) = b(i-1) +\n641\t   |slice(i)|`.\"\n642\t  [lx k]\n643\t  (reduce (fn [[frames st] f]\n644\t            (let [seg (payload-segment lx f)\n645\t                  pc (:pc f)\n646\t                  st (into st (layout-slice lx seg pc (:window f)))\n647\t                  store-of (engine/env-store-of (:env f))]\n648\t              [(conj frames (cond-> {:return-pc (+ (offset :stack (:kernel lx) seg) (a->h seg (dec pc)) 1)\n649\t                                     :frames (lower-frames lx seg pc (:env f))\n650\t                                     :stack-base (count st)}\n651\t                              (some? store-of) (assoc :store-of store-of)))\n652\t               st]))\n653\t          [[] []]\n654\t          k))\n655\t\n656\t\n657\t(defn- lower-stack\n658\t  [lx p fill]\n659\t  (let [k (:kernel lx)\n660\t        seg (payload-segment lx p)\n661\t        off (offset :stack k seg)\n662\t        [frames st] (stack-k lx (:k p))\n663\t        common {:segment (:segment k) :format stack/format-tag :hash (:hash k) :image (:stack-id seg)\n664\t                :continuation frames}]\n665\t    (if (contains? p :site)\n666\t      (cond-> (merge common {:pc (+ off (a->h seg (:site p)) 1) :resume-mode :return-result\n667\t                             :stack st :frames (get fill :frames [])})\n668\t        (some? (:store-of fill)) (assoc :store-of (:store-of fill)))\n669\t      (let [pc (:pc p)\n670\t            store-of (engine/env-store-of (:env p))]\n671\t        (cond-> (merge common {:pc (+ off (a->h seg (dec pc)) 1)\n672\t                               :frames (lower-frames lx seg pc (:env p))\n673\t                               :stack (into st (layout-slice lx seg pc (:window p)))})\n674\t          (some? store-of) (assoc :store-of store-of))))))\n675\t\n676\t\n677\t(def ^:private canonical-keys\n678\t  #{:segment :pc :site :env :window :k :deliver :type :id})\n679\t\n680\t\n681\t(defn lower-state\n682\t  \"Canonical act or tail payload `p` as the receiving kernel's entry\n683\t   (§4.2, §4.3), engine fields carried. `fill` gives a lowered tail's\n684\t   `:frames`/`:store-of` (default `[]`/nil), which the return transition\n685\t   replaces unread (§5.6 item 8).\"\n686\t  ([lx p] (lower-state lx p {}))\n687\t  ([lx p fill]\n688\t   (let [fields (apply dissoc p canonical-keys)]\n689\t     (merge (cond-> fields (contains? fields :datom) (update :datom #(positional-value lx %)))\n690\t            (if (= :stack (:kind lx)) (lower-stack lx p fill) (lower-register lx p fill))))))\n691\t\n692\t\n693\t(defn lower-context\n694\t  \"The lower context into kernel `k` over `space`; `address` maps a\n695\t   payload's or closure's `:segment` to A (default: it is A).\"\n696\t  ([k space] (lower-context k space identity))\n697\t  ([k space address]\n698\t   (assoc {} :kind (kernel-kind k) :kernel k :space space :free-env (or (:free-env k) {})\n699\t          :owner (:owner k) :address address)))\n700\t\n701\t\n702\t;; =============================================================================\n703\t;; Tasks\n704\t;; =============================================================================\n705\t\n706\t(defn- holds-procedure?\n707\t  \"Whether kernel value `x` is or holds, through guest collections, a\n708\t   closure or continuation.\"\n709\t  [x]\n710\t  (cond\n711\t    (or (values/closure? x) (values/continuation? x)) true\n712\t    (values/host-typed? x) false\n713\t    (map? x) (boolean (some holds-procedure? (concat (keys x) (vals x))))\n714\t    (coll? x) (boolean (some holds-procedure? x))\n715\t    :else false))\n716\t\n717\t\n718\t(defn canonical-task\n719\t  \"Quiescent kernel `k` presented as semantic-register machine `template`\n720\t   (a fresh machine of the same composition) for `rows/lift-task`: code\n721\t   by A from `space`, every wait, parked record and value reconstructed\n722\t   through the layout; resources, stores and counters carried. A running\n723\t   kernel is `:yin.k/not-at-safepoint`; install children are not carried\n724\t   by this phase's layouts; a closure or continuation in the free\n725\t   environment has no finite canonical form (§6.3).\"\n726\t  [k space template]\n727\t  (when (engine/active-continuation? k)\n728\t    (refuse! :yin.k/not-at-safepoint nil {:yin.k/pc (:pc k)}))\n729\t  (when (seq (:installs k))\n730\t    (refuse! :yin.k/unsupported :installs {:yin.k/names (vec (keys (:installs k)))}))\n731\t  (when-let [sym (some (fn [[sym x]] (when (holds-procedure? x) sym)) (sort-by (comp str key) (:free-env k)))]\n732\t    (refuse! :yin.k/non-portable :free-env-value {:yin.k/key sym}))\n733\t  (let [cx (lift-context k space (:owner template))\n734\t        conv #(canonical-value cx %)\n735\t        parked (into {} (map (fn [[id rec]] [id (assoc (lift-state cx rec) :type :parked-continuation :id id)]))\n736\t                     (:parked k))\n737\t        value (:value k)\n738\t        parked-value? (and (map? value) (= :parked-continuation (:type value)) (contains? parked (:id value)))\n739\t        code (into {} (map (fn [[a s]] [a (assoc {} :vector (:vector s) :address a :analysis (:analysis s))]))\n740\t                   (:segments space))]\n741\t    (assoc template\n742\t           :code code\n743\t           :code-aliases (into {} (map (fn [a] [a a])) (keys code))\n744\t           :program nil :control nil :window {} :k nil\n745\t           :resources (:resources k)\n746\t           :capability-secret (:capability-secret k)\n747\t           :free-env (:free-env k)\n748\t           :env (or (:free-env k) {})\n749\t           :store (conv (:store k))\n750\t           :module-stores (conv (or (:module-stores k) {}))\n751\t           :parked parked\n752\t           :wait-set (mapv #(lift-state cx %) (:wait-set k))\n753\t           :ready-queue (:ready-queue k)\n754\t           :value (if parked-value? (get parked (:id value)) (conv value))\n755\t           :id-counter (:id-counter k)\n756\t           :installs {}\n757\t           :halted? (:halted? k)\n758\t           :blocked? (:blocked? k))))\n759\t\n760\t\n761\t(defn lift-task\n762\t  \"§7.1 for a de Bruijn kernel: `rows/lift-task` over its canonical\n763\t   presentation. `template` is a fresh semantic-register machine of the\n764\t   kernel's composition; opts as rows/lift-task's.\"\n765\t  [k space template serve! opts]\n766\t  (rows/lift-task (canonical-task k space template) serve! opts))\n767\t\n768\t\n769\t(defn attach-space\n770\t  \"Kernel `k` holding the derived image of every segment of `space`, in\n771\t   A order (§7.2: derive and attach the image for each A).\"\n772\t  [k space]\n773\t  (let [kind (kernel-kind k)]\n774\t    (reduce (fn [k a]\n775\t              (let [seg (segment-of space a)]\n776\t                (if (= :stack kind)\n777\t                  (stack/attach-image k (:stack seg) vm/stack-contract)\n778\t                  (register/attach-image k (:register seg) vm/register-contract))))\n779\t            k\n780\t            (sort-by str (keys (:segments space))))))\n781\t\n782\t\n783\t(defn machine-space\n784\t  \"The space of the A vectors semantic-register machine `m` holds, and\n785\t   the map from its segment ids to A.\"\n786\t  [m]\n787\t  [(space (map :vector (vals (:code m))))\n788\t   (fn [seg] (or (get-in m [:code seg :address]) (when (contains? (:code-aliases m) seg) seg)))])\n789\t\n790\t\n791\t(defn kernel-task\n792\t  \"Step 12 for a de Bruijn receiver: semantic-register machine `m` (what\n793\t   `rows/lower-task` restored) as fresh kernel `k` of the same\n794\t   composition: every image derived and attached, the free environment\n795\t   set, every wait, parked record and value lowered through the layout.\n796\t   Delivers nothing, runs nothing.\"\n797\t  [m k]\n798\t  (let [[sp address] (machine-space m)\n799\t        k (attach-space k sp)\n800\t        lx (lower-context k sp address)\n801\t        conv #(positional-value lx %)\n802\t        parked (into {} (map (fn [[id rec]] [id (assoc (lower-state lx rec) :type :parked-continuation :id id)]))\n803\t                     (:parked m))\n804\t        value (:value m)\n805\t        parked-value? (and (map? value) (= :parked-continuation (:type value)) (contains? parked (:id value)))]\n806\t    (assoc k\n807\t           :resources (:resources m)\n808\t           :free-env (:free-env m)\n809\t           :store (conv (:store m))\n810\t           :module-stores (conv (or (:module-stores m) {}))\n811\t           :parked parked\n812\t           :wait-set (mapv #(lower-state lx %) (:wait-set m))\n813\t           :ready-queue []\n814\t           :value (if parked-value? (get parked (:id value)) (conv value))\n815\t           :id-counter (:id-counter m)\n816\t           :halted? (:halted? m)\n817\t           :blocked? (:blocked? m))))\n818\t\n819\t\n820\t(defn- lexical-names\n821\t  \"The names the chain binds at `pc` of `v`.\"\n822\t  [v pc]\n823\t  (let [bodies (code/body-ranges v)]\n824\t    (loop [b (code/body-index bodies pc) out #{}]\n825\t      (if-let [owner (:owner (nth bodies b))]\n826\t        (recur (code/body-index bodies owner) (into out (nth (nth v owner) 2)))\n827\t        out))))\n828\t\n829\t\n830\t(declare state-prim)\n831\t\n832\t\n833\t(defn- value-prim\n834\t  \"The path to the first `:prim` row carrier value `x` reaches as kernel\n835\t   payload data: through guest collections, a closure's lexical bindings\n836\t   (its positional frames) and a capture's state; or nil.\"\n837\t  [code x path]\n838\t  (when (and (vector? x) (= :row (first x)))\n839\t    (let [n (second x) ss (:slots n)]\n840\t      (case (:kind n)\n841\t        :prim path\n842\t        (:vec :list :set :map) (some (fn [[i y]] (value-prim code y (conj path i))) (map-indexed vector ss))\n843\t        :closure (let [[a entry _ bindings] ss\n844\t                       v (get code a)\n845\t                       owner (when v (some (fn [pc]\n846\t                                             (let [t (nth v pc)]\n847\t                                               (when (and (= :closure (nth t 0)) (= entry (nth t 3))) pc)))\n848\t                                           (range (count v))))\n849\t                       names (if owner (lexical-names v owner) #{})]\n850\t                   (some (fn [[s y]] (when (contains? names s) (value-prim code y (conj path s))))\n851\t                         (partition 2 (:slots bindings))))\n852\t        :reified (state-prim code (first ss) (conj path 0))\n853\t        nil))))\n854\t\n855\t\n856\t(defn- frame-prim\n857\t  \"A frame's window and lexical bindings (§4.4: the free part is the\n858\t   kernel's :free-env, never payload data).\"\n859\t  [code a pc e w path]\n860\t  (let [names (lexical-names (get code a) pc)]\n861\t    (or (some (fn [[r y]] (value-prim code y (conj path :window r))) (partition 2 (:slots w)))\n862\t        (some (fn [[sym y]] (when (contains? names sym) (value-prim code y (conj path :env sym))))\n863\t              (partition 2 (:slots (first (:slots e))))))))\n864\t\n865\t\n866\t(defn- state-prim\n867\t  [code n path]\n868\t  (let [kframes (fn [k]\n869\t                  (some (fn [[i f]]\n870\t                          (let [[a pc e w] (:slots f)]\n871\t                            (frame-prim code a pc e w (conj path :k i))))\n872\t                        (map-indexed vector (:slots k))))\n873\t        [a pc e w k] (:slots n)]\n874\t    (case (:kind n)\n875\t      :act (or (frame-prim code a pc e w path) (kframes k))\n876\t      :tail (kframes e)\n877\t      nil)))\n878\t\n879\t\n880\t(defn- row-procedure\n881\t  \"The path to the first closure or continuation row carrier value `x`\n882\t   holds, through guest collections; or nil.\"\n883\t  [x path]\n884\t  (when (and (vector? x) (= :row (first x)))\n885\t    (let [n (second x)]\n886\t      (case (:kind n)\n887\t        (:closure :reified) path\n888\t        (:vec :list :set :map) (some (fn [[i y]] (row-procedure y (conj path i))) (map-indexed vector (:slots n)))\n889\t        nil))))\n890\t\n891\t\n892\t(defn- free-env-procedure\n893\t  \"§6.3: a de Bruijn kernel resolves free names through its one\n894\t   `free-env` while a canonical closure snapshots its `env`, so a closure\n895\t   or continuation held in the free environment has no finite canonical\n896\t   form there. The path `[:free-env sym …]` to the first such value of\n897\t   decoded task `task`, or nil.\"\n898\t  [task]\n899\t  (some (fn [[sym x]] (row-procedure x [:free-env sym]))\n900\t        (partition 2 (:slots (nth (:slots task) 5)))))\n901\t\n902\t\n903\t(defn- image-collision\n904\t  \"§4.1: `[ident #{A …}]` for the first image of kind `kind` two carried A\n905\t   derive, or nil. A de Bruijn kernel attaches one image once, so it\n906\t   cannot hold both segments; no enumeration order selects an A. A\n907\t   vector that derives no image is left to the carrier's own checks.\"\n908\t  [code kind]\n909\t  (let [ident (fn [a v]\n910\t                (try\n911\t                  (if (= :stack kind)\n912\t                    (dcode/image-hash (:image (derive/stack-image v)))\n913\t                    (rcode/register-hash (derive/register-image v)))\n914\t                  (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _ [::underivable a])))\n915\t        by-image (reduce (fn [acc [a v]] (update acc (ident a v) (fnil conj #{}) a)) {} code)]\n916\t    (some (fn [[i as]] (when (< 1 (count as)) [i as])) (sort-by (comp str key) by-image))))\n917\t\n918\t\n919\t(defn lower-defect\n920\t  \"What a kernel of `kind` cannot hold, judged on decoded task `task`\n921\t   before anything is attached: two carried A of one image (§4.1), install\n922\t   children (not carried by this phase's layouts), a closure or\n923\t   continuation in the free environment (§6.3), and for the register\n924\t   kernel a primitive function in the payload data of a wait or parked\n925\t   state (a window, a lexical binding, or reached through them), which\n926\t   its restore refuses as `:continuation-registers` (`vm/machine-data?`).\n927\t   nil when it can.\"\n928\t  [task kind]\n929\t  (let [slots (:slots task)\n930\t        code (nth slots 11)\n931\t        collision (image-collision code kind)\n932\t        free (free-env-procedure task)]\n933\t    (cond\n934\t      collision\n935\t      (assoc {} :yin.k/status :yin.k/unsupported :yin.k/kind :ambiguous-image\n936\t             :yin.k/image (first collision) :yin.k/segments (second collision))\n937\t\n938\t      (seq (nth slots 12))\n939\t      (assoc {} :yin.k/status :yin.k/unsupported :yin.k/kind :installs)\n940\t\n941\t      free\n942\t      (assoc {} :yin.k/status :yin.k/unsupported :yin.k/kind :free-env-value :yin.k/path free)\n943\t\n944\t      (= :register kind)\n945\t      (when-let [path (or (some (fn [[i w]] (state-prim code (first (:slots w)) [:frames i]))\n946\t                                (map-indexed vector (nth slots 13)))\n947\t                          (some (fn [[p st]] (state-prim code st [:parked p]))\n948\t                                (partition 2 (:slots (nth slots 8)))))]\n949\t        (assoc {} :yin.k/status :yin.k/unsupported :yin.k/kind :continuation-registers :yin.k/path path))\n950\t\n951\t      :else nil)))\n952\t\n953\t\n954\t(defn lower-task\n955\t  \"§7.2 into a de Bruijn kernel: decode `wire`, refuse what kernel `k`\n956\t   cannot hold (`lower-defect`) before any attach, then `rows/lower-task`\n957\t   into `scratch` (a fresh semantic-register machine of the same\n958\t   composition: the carrier's steps 1-11 and restore) and `kernel-task`\n959\t   into `k`. Throws the first refusal as ex-data.\"\n960\t  ([scratch k wire attach!] (lower-task scratch k wire attach! {}))\n961\t  ([scratch k wire attach! opts]\n962\t   (let [task (rows/decode wire (merge rows/default-budget (:budget opts)))]\n963\t     (when (= :task (:kind task))\n964\t       (when-let [d (lower-defect task (kernel-kind k))]\n965\t         (throw (ex-info \"Layout refused\" d))))\n966\t     (kernel-task (rows/lower-task scratch wire attach! opts) k))))\n967\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"47508f4a-f118-4fad-b5f9-49922c52f330","uuid":"2ca1b723-20ed-485d-9e7e-3f438fe9351d","timestamp":"2026-10-13T08:29:48.444Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/.claude/projects/-Users-sto-workspace-datomworld-docs-6c/47508f4a-f118-4fad-b5f9-49922c52f330/tool-results/b9028g8p3.txt","content":"781a9ba8 Merge branch 'srvm-phase6c': slice 6c, the register and stack layouts and the cross-engine lanes of the safepoint harness\n30730c51 test(yin.vm.semantic-register): scoped native layout worlds, guarded law-4 controls, nested free-environment refusals, receiver image functions pinned (phase 6c review)\ndc545aaa fix(yin.vm.semantic-register): layout refusals for ambiguous images and free-environment procedures, law-4 controls, an ambiguous virt refusal, audit allowlist (phase 6c review)\n(ns yin.vm.semantic-register.layout\n  \"Phase 6c (docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md §4):\n   the de Bruijn register and stack kernels reconstruct the canonical\n   frame of the register machine through their layouts, and lower it\n   back.\n\n   Static half, per segment A: `segment` derives R(A) and H(A) and reads\n   off the register pairing (`phys`, the restricted inverse `virt`, the\n   kernel's `live` as live-out with tail boundaries `[]`), the stack\n   correspondence (`h->a`, `a->h`, every `:push` removed) and the operand\n   layout `stack-layout` (the values pushed and not yet consumed while\n   control is inside a pc's expression). A `space` indexes segments by\n   the kernels' image identities, R and H, which are checksums: A is the\n   only code identity.\n\n   Dynamic half: `lift-state` reads a kernel's wait entry, parked record\n   or reified payload as the canonical `act` or `tail` payload the\n   semantic-register evaluator mints (`{:segment A :pc :env :window :k\n   :deliver}`, `{:segment A :site :k :deliver}`, engine fields carried);\n   `lower-state` is its inverse. The register kernel's return\n   destinations are recovered from A, never from the physical `:dest`;\n   the stack kernel's operand stack is sliced `[previous-base, base)` per\n   frame and lowered with cumulative bases. `E` is the free environment\n   merged under the chain's positional frames (§4.4); the inverse reads\n   each frame back from `E` by the chain, never the free environment.\n\n   Task level: `canonical-task` presents a quiescent kernel as a\n   semantic-register machine for `yin.vm.ucf.rows/lift-task`;\n   `kernel-task` restores a machine `rows/lower-task` produced into a\n   fresh kernel; `lift-task` and `lower-task` compose them with the row\n   carrier, the lower refusing what a kernel cannot hold before any\n   stream is attached. A layout never runs code, never fills a binding\n   from the receiver and never invents a safepoint (§4.5).\"\n  (:require [dao.jing :as jing]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn-code :as dcode]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn-register-code :as rcode]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn.register :as register]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn.stack :as stack]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\n            [yin.vm.module :as module]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.analysis :as analysis]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.code :as code]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.derive :as derive]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.rows :as rows]\n            [yin.vm.values :as values]))\n\n\n(defn- refuse!\n  [status kind data]\n  (throw (ex-info \"Layout refused\" (merge data (assoc {} :yin.k/status status :yin.k/kind kind)))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Static half: one segment\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- operands\n  \"The register operands of an A tuple, destination first, then its uses\n   in table order.\"\n  [t]\n  (into (if-some [r (code/rd t)] [r] []) (code/uses t)))\n\n\n(defn- register-operands\n  \"The `:reg`/`:regs` operands of an R tuple in table order (the `:live`\n   slot is `:data`, never paired).\"\n  [t]\n  (into []\n        (mapcat (fn [[[_ kind] x]] (case kind :reg [x] :regs x [])))\n        (map vector (get rcode/opcode-table (nth t 0)) (rest t))))\n\n\n(defn register-pairs\n  \"`[pc virtual physical]` for every register operand of every pc: A's\n   tuple and R's name their registers in the same slots (phase-5 §2.4).\"\n  [v image]\n  (into []\n        (mapcat (fn [pc]\n                  (map (fn [x s] [pc x s])\n                       (operands (nth v pc))\n                       (register-operands (nth (:instructions image) pc)))))\n        (range (count v))))\n\n\n(defn- phys-maps\n  \"Per body, `{virtual physical}` read off the pairs; the first pc that\n   names a virtual wins (register-pairing checks they agree).\"\n  [bodies pairs]\n  (reduce (fn [acc [pc x s]]\n            (let [b (code/body-index bodies pc)]\n              (if (contains? (nth acc b) x) acc (assoc-in acc [b x] s))))\n          (vec (repeat (count bodies) {}))\n          pairs))\n\n\n(defn correspondence\n  \"§4.3 static item 1: H with every `:push` removed corresponds one to one,\n   in order, with A. Answers `{:a->h [h-pc …] :h->a {h-pc a-pc}}`.\"\n  [h]\n  (reduce (fn [acc hpc]\n            (if (= :push (nth (nth h hpc) 0))\n              acc\n              (-> acc\n                  (update :a->h conj hpc)\n                  (assoc-in [:h->a hpc] (count (:a->h acc))))))\n          {:a->h [] :h->a {}}\n          (range (count h))))\n\n\n(def ^:private pushing-ops\n  \"The parse nodes whose children before the current one are pushed:\n   `:call` (the operator and earlier operands), `:ffi-call` (earlier\n   operands) and `:stream-put` (the target, while the value runs).\"\n  #{:call :ffi-call :stream-put})\n\n\n(defn- stack-layouts\n  \"§4.3 static item 2 for every pc of every body: `{pc [virtual …]}`,\n   bottom to top, over the parse tree's ancestors outermost first.\"\n  [v bodies]\n  (letfn [(walk\n            [out node pending]\n            (let [out (assoc out (:pc node) pending)\n                  pushes? (contains? pushing-ops (:op node))\n                  uses (when pushes? (code/uses (nth v (:pc node))))]\n              (reduce (fn [out [i child]]\n                        (walk out child (if pushes? (into pending (take i uses)) pending)))\n                      out\n                      (map-indexed vector (:children node)))))]\n    (reduce (fn [out body] (walk out (:expr body) [])) {} bodies)))\n\n\n(defn segment\n  \"The static facts of one admitted A vector `v`, for both kernels.\"\n  [v]\n  (let [bodies (code/parse v)\n        r (derive/register-image v)\n        h (:image (derive/stack-image v))\n        pairs (register-pairs v r)]\n    (merge {:vector v\n            :address (jing/segment-key v)\n            :bodies bodies\n            :analysis (analysis/analyze v)\n            :register r\n            :register-id (rcode/register-hash r)\n            :stack h\n            :stack-id (dcode/image-hash h)\n            :pairs pairs\n            :phys (phys-maps bodies pairs)\n            :layouts (stack-layouts v bodies)}\n           (correspondence h))))\n\n\n(defn space\n  \"Segments by A, and A by each kernel's image identity. `segments` is a\n   seq of `segment` results or of A vectors.\"\n  [segments]\n  (reduce (fn [acc s]\n            (let [s (if (map? s) s (segment s))\n                  a (:address s)]\n              (-> acc\n                  (assoc-in [:segments a] s)\n                  (update-in [:register (:register-id s)] (fnil conj #{}) a)\n                  (update-in [:stack (:stack-id s)] (fnil conj #{}) a))))\n          {:segments {} :register {} :stack {}}\n          segments))\n\n\n(defn segment-of\n  \"The segment A names in `space`.\"\n  [space a]\n  (or (get-in space [:segments a])\n      (refuse! :yin.k/unsatisfied :segment {:yin.k/segment a})))\n\n\n(defn- image-segment\n  \"The segment whose `kind` image is `ident`: an identity is a checksum,\n   so two A deriving one image are ambiguous and refused.\"\n  [space kind ident]\n  (let [as (get-in space [kind ident])]\n    (cond\n      (empty? as) (refuse! :yin.k/non-portable :unknown-image {:yin.k/image ident})\n      (< 1 (count as)) (refuse! :yin.k/non-portable :ambiguous-image {:yin.k/image ident})\n      :else (segment-of space (first as)))))\n\n\n(defn- inst\n  [seg pc]\n  (nth (:vector seg) pc))\n\n\n(defn- body-of\n  [seg pc]\n  (code/body-index (:bodies seg) pc))\n\n\n(defn phys\n  \"`phys(body(pc), x)`: the physical register R names for virtual `x` in\n   the body holding `pc`.\"\n  [seg pc x]\n  (let [s (get (nth (:phys seg) (body-of seg pc)) x)]\n    (when (nil? s) (refuse! :yin.k/non-portable :register-layout {:yin.k/pc pc :yin.k/register x}))\n    s))\n\n\n(defn live-out\n  \"`live-out*(p)`: the union of `L(q)` over p's actual successors (empty\n   for a tail call).\"\n  [seg p]\n  (reduce (fn [acc q] (into acc (analysis/live (:analysis seg) q)))\n          #{}\n          (analysis/successors (:vector seg) p)))\n\n\n(defn register-live\n  \"§5.6 item 3: the `live` operand R must carry at boundary `p`,\n   `(sort (map phys (disj live-out*(p) rd)))`, the destination removed as\n   a virtual id before mapping; `[]` at a tail call.\"\n  [seg p]\n  (vec (sort (map #(phys seg p %) (disj (live-out seg p) (code/rd (inst seg p)))))))\n\n\n(defn virt\n  \"The restricted inverse of `phys` at boundary `p`: the virtual of\n   `live-out*(p)` held in physical `s`. A slot outside that image (only a\n   tampered entry names one) reads as the one virtual of the body R maps\n   there, so the frame validator judges the window; an ambiguous slot is\n   refused.\"\n  [seg p s]\n  (let [m (nth (:phys seg) (body-of seg p))\n        live (filterv #(= s (get m %)) (sort (live-out seg p)))\n        named (filterv #(= s (get m %)) (sort (keys m)))]\n    (cond\n      (= 1 (count live)) (first live)\n      (and (empty? live) (= 1 (count named))) (first named)\n      :else (refuse! :yin.k/non-portable :register-layout {:yin.k/pc p :yin.k/register s}))))\n\n\n(defn stack-layout\n  \"§4.3: the virtual registers pushed and not yet consumed while control\n   is inside the expression at A pc `p`, bottom to top.\"\n  [seg p]\n  (get (:layouts seg) p))\n\n\n(defn chain\n  \"The closure pcs owning the body that holds `pc`, outermost first.\"\n  [seg pc]\n  (loop [b (body-of seg pc) out ()]\n    (if-let [owner (:owner (nth (:bodies seg) b))]\n      (recur (body-of seg owner) (conj out owner))\n      (vec out))))\n\n\n(defn- params\n  [seg c]\n  (nth (inst seg c) 2))\n\n\n(defn env-of\n  \"§4.4 forward: `E` at `pc` from the positional frames `F` (outermost\n   first, values already canonical), the task's free environment and the\n   activation's module store.\"\n  [seg pc free-env frames store-of]\n  (let [cs (chain seg pc)]\n    (when-not (= (count cs) (count frames))\n      (refuse! :yin.k/non-portable :frame-depth {:yin.k/pc pc :yin.k/depth (count frames)}))\n    (cond-> (reduce (fn [e [c f]] (merge e (engine/bind-params (params seg c) f)))\n                    (or free-env {})\n                    (map vector cs frames))\n      (some? store-of) (assoc engine/store-of-key store-of))))\n\n\n(defn frames-of\n  \"§4.4 inverse: `F[i] = (mapv #(get E %) params(cᵢ))` over the chain at\n   `pc`. An outer value a shadowing inner binder hides reads as the inner\n   one; the canonical frame never held it.\"\n  [seg pc env]\n  (mapv (fn [c] (mapv #(get env %) (params seg c))) (chain seg pc)))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Kernel dispatch\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn kernel-kind\n  \"`:stack` or `:register`, by the kernel's link format.\"\n  [k]\n  (let [f (when (satisfies? module/IModuleKernel k) (:format (module/link-format k)))]\n    (cond\n      (= stack/format-tag f) :stack\n      (= register/format-tag f) :register\n      :else (refuse! :yin.k/unsupported :kernel {:yin.k/format f}))))\n\n\n(defn- image-pc\n  \"`[segment rel-pc]` of absolute kernel pc `pc`.\"\n  [kind k space pc]\n  (let [[ident rel] (or (if (= :stack kind) (stack/image-pc k pc) (register/image-pc k pc))\n                        (refuse! :yin.k/non-portable :unknown-image {:yin.k/pc pc}))]\n    [(image-segment space kind ident) rel]))\n\n\n(defn offset\n  \"The offset of segment `seg`'s image in kernel `k`'s code space.\"\n  [kind k seg]\n  (let [ident (if (= :stack kind) (:stack-id seg) (:register-id seg))]\n    (or (if (= :stack kind) (stack/absolute-pc k [ident 0]) (register/absolute-pc k [ident 0]))\n        (refuse! :yin.k/unsatisfied :image-not-attached {:yin.k/segment (:address seg)}))))\n\n\n(def ^:private parking-ops\n  \"A1: the instructions a resume pc may follow, besides a non-tail call.\"\n  #{:stream-next :stream-put :ffi-call :park :current-continuation})\n\n\n(defn- safepoint!\n  \"Refuse `:yin.k/not-at-safepoint` unless the A instruction before `pc`\n   parks (a tail call for a tail state): a layout never invents a\n   safepoint (§4.5).\"\n  [seg pc tail?]\n  (let [t (when (and (integer? pc) (< 0 pc) (<= pc (count (:vector seg)))) (inst seg (dec pc)))\n        op (when t (nth t 0))]\n    (when-not (and t\n                   (= (body-of seg (dec pc)) (body-of seg (min pc (dec (count (:vector seg))))))\n                   (if tail?\n                     (code/tail-call? t)\n                     (or (contains? parking-ops op) (and (= :call op) (not (code/tail-call? t))))))\n      (refuse! :yin.k/not-at-safepoint nil {:yin.k/pc pc}))))\n\n\n(defn- h->a\n  \"The A pc of H pc `hpc`; a `:push` has none and is no safepoint.\"\n  [seg hpc]\n  (or (get (:h->a seg) hpc) (refuse! :yin.k/not-at-safepoint nil {:yin.k/pc hpc})))\n\n\n(defn- a->h\n  [seg pc]\n  (nth (:a->h seg) pc))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Values: positional closures and kernel continuations, both ways\n;; =============================================================================\n;;\n;; A lift context `cx` is {:kind :kernel :space :free-env :owner}; a lower\n;; context `lx` adds :address, naming a canonical payload's or closure's\n;; :segment as A.\n\n(declare lift-state lower-state canonical-value positional-value)\n\n\n(defn- walk-value\n  \"`x` with its guest collections rebuilt around `f`, which converts\n   closures and continuations.\"\n  [f x]\n  (cond\n    (values/host-typed? x) (f x)\n    (map? x) (into {} (map (fn [[k v]] [(walk-value f k) (walk-value f v)])) x)\n    (vector? x) (mapv #(walk-value f %) x)\n    (set? x) (into #{} (map #(walk-value f %)) x)\n    (seq? x) (apply list (map #(walk-value f %) x))\n    :else x))\n\n\n(defn- canonical-closure\n  \"§4.4: a positional closure as the canonical `{:type :closure :params\n   :entry :segment :env}`: `params` from A's `:closure` at the owner of\n   the entry body, `env` by the forward rule over the closure's frames.\"\n  [cx c]\n  (let [[seg rel] (image-pc (:kind cx) (:kernel cx) (:space cx) (:body-pc c))\n        entry (if (= :stack (:kind cx)) (h->a seg rel) rel)\n        owner (:owner (nth (:bodies seg) (body-of seg entry)))\n        _ (when-not (and owner (= entry (nth (inst seg owner) 3)))\n            (refuse! :yin.k/non-portable :closure-origin {:yin.k/entry entry}))\n        ps (params seg owner)]\n    (when-not (= (count ps) (:arity c))\n      (refuse! :yin.k/non-portable :closure-binders {:yin.k/entry entry}))\n    {:type :closure :params ps :entry entry :segment (:address seg)\n     :env (env-of seg owner (:free-env cx)\n                  (mapv (fn [f] (mapv #(canonical-value cx %) f)) (:frames c))\n                  (:store-of c))}))\n\n\n(defn- canonical-value*\n  [cx x]\n  (cond\n    (values/closure? x) (values/closure (:owner cx) (canonical-closure cx (values/payload x)))\n    (values/continuation? x)\n    (values/continuation (:owner cx) (assoc (lift-state cx (values/payload x)) :type :reified-continuation))\n    :else x))\n\n\n(defn canonical-value\n  \"Kernel value `x` with every positional closure and kernel continuation\n   reconstructed canonically (cx: a lift context).\"\n  [cx x]\n  (walk-value #(canonical-value* cx %) x))\n\n\n(defn- address-of\n  [lx seg-id]\n  (let [a ((:address lx) seg-id)]\n    (when (nil? a) (refuse! :yin.k/non-portable :unaddressed-segment {:yin.k/hint seg-id}))\n    a))\n\n\n(defn- positional-closure\n  \"The inverse of canonical-closure: the entry's absolute pc in the\n   receiving kernel, the frames read back from `env` by the owner's chain.\"\n  [lx c]\n  (let [seg (segment-of (:space lx) (address-of lx (:segment c)))\n        entry (:entry c)\n        owner (:owner (nth (:bodies seg) (body-of seg entry)))\n        store-of (engine/env-store-of (:env c))]\n    (when-not (and owner (= entry (nth (inst seg owner) 3)) (= (vec (:params c)) (vec (params seg owner))))\n      (refuse! :yin.k/undecodable :closure-binders {:yin.k/entry entry}))\n    (cond-> {:type :closure :arity (count (:params c))\n             :body-pc (+ (offset (:kind lx) (:kernel lx) seg) (if (= :stack (:kind lx)) (a->h seg entry) entry))\n             :frames (mapv (fn [f] (mapv #(positional-value lx %) f)) (frames-of seg owner (:env c)))}\n      (some? store-of) (assoc :store-of store-of))))\n\n\n(defn- positional-value*\n  [lx x]\n  (cond\n    (values/closure? x) (values/closure (:owner lx) (positional-closure lx (values/payload x)))\n    (values/continuation? x)\n    (values/continuation (:owner lx) (merge {:type :reified-continuation} (lower-state lx (values/payload x))))\n    :else x))\n\n\n(defn positional-value\n  \"Canonical value `x` with every closure and continuation lowered into\n   the receiving kernel (lx: a lower context).\"\n  [lx x]\n  (walk-value #(positional-value* lx %) x))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Lift: a kernel payload as the canonical act or tail\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(def ^:private kernel-keys\n  \"The register payload keys of either kernel; every other key of an\n   entry is the engine's and travels in the pending.\"\n  #{:segment :site-pc :pc :frames :regs :live :continuation :dest :resume-mode\n    :format :hash :image :images :store-of :stack})\n\n\n(defn- canonical-env\n  [cx seg pc frames store-of]\n  (env-of seg pc (:free-env cx) (mapv (fn [f] (mapv #(canonical-value cx %) f)) frames) store-of))\n\n\n(defn- register-window\n  \"§4.2 step 4: `{virt(site, s) V}` over the entry's `[s V]` pairs.\"\n  [cx seg site regs]\n  (into {} (map (fn [[s x]] [(virt seg site s) (canonical-value cx x)])) regs))\n\n\n(defn- register-kframe\n  \"§4.2 step 6, one frame independently: its own image row and A, `rd`\n   from A, never the physical `:dest`.\"\n  [cx f]\n  (let [[seg pc] (image-pc :register (:kernel cx) (:space cx) (:return-pc f))]\n    (safepoint! seg pc false)\n    {:type :return :segment (:address seg) :pc pc\n     :env (canonical-env cx seg pc (:frames f) (:store-of f))\n     :window (register-window cx seg (dec pc) (:regs f))\n     :rd (code/rd (inst seg (dec pc)))}))\n\n\n(defn- lift-register\n  [cx entry]\n  (let [[seg pc] (image-pc :register (:kernel cx) (:space cx) (:pc entry))\n        tail? (= :return-result (:resume-mode entry))\n        _ (safepoint! seg pc tail?)\n        k (mapv #(register-kframe cx %) (:continuation entry))]\n    (if tail?\n      {:segment (:address seg) :site (dec pc) :k k :deliver {:deliver :return}}\n      {:segment (:address seg) :pc pc\n       :env (canonical-env cx seg pc (:frames entry) (:store-of entry))\n       :window (register-window cx seg (dec pc) (:regs entry))\n       :k k\n       :deliver {:deliver :rd :rd (code/rd (inst seg (dec pc)))}})))\n\n\n(defn slices\n  \"§4.3's K slices of operand stack `st` under return frames whose bases\n   are `bases`, outermost first: `St[b(i-1), b(i))` per frame with\n   `b(-1) = 0`, then the current activation's `St[b(m-1), n)`.\"\n  [st bases]\n  (let [bounds (into [0] bases)]\n    (conj (mapv (fn [lo hi] (subvec st lo hi)) bounds (rest bounds))\n          (subvec st (peek bounds) (count st)))))\n\n\n(defn- slice-window\n  \"`(zipmap (stack-layout (dec pc)) slice)`; the two have equal length.\"\n  [cx seg pc slice]\n  (let [layout (stack-layout seg (dec pc))]\n    (when-not (= (count layout) (count slice))\n      (refuse! :yin.k/non-portable :stack-layout {:yin.k/pc pc :yin.k/layout layout :yin.k/slice (count slice)}))\n    (zipmap layout (map #(canonical-value cx %) slice))))\n\n\n(defn- stack-site\n  \"`[segment site]`: the A pc of the parking instruction before absolute\n   stack resume pc `abs`.\"\n  [cx abs]\n  (let [[seg rel] (image-pc :stack (:kernel cx) (:space cx) abs)]\n    [seg (h->a seg (dec rel))]))\n\n\n(defn- lift-stack\n  [cx entry]\n  (let [st (vec (:stack entry))\n        frames (vec (:continuation entry))\n        bases (mapv :stack-base frames)\n        _ (when-not (and (every? integer? bases) (apply <= 0 (conj bases (count st))))\n            (refuse! :yin.k/non-portable :stack-base {:yin.k/bases bases}))\n        parts (slices st bases)\n        [seg site] (stack-site cx (:pc entry))\n        tail? (code/tail-call? (inst seg site))\n        _ (safepoint! seg (inc site) tail?)\n        k (mapv (fn [f slice]\n                  (let [[fseg fsite] (stack-site cx (:return-pc f))\n                        pc (inc fsite)]\n                    (safepoint! fseg pc false)\n                    {:type :return :segment (:address fseg) :pc pc\n                     :env (canonical-env cx fseg pc (:frames f) (:store-of f))\n                     :window (slice-window cx fseg pc slice)\n                     :rd (code/rd (inst fseg fsite))}))\n                frames parts)]\n    (if tail?\n      ;; frozen §2.4: the current frames, store-of and slice are dead\n      {:segment (:address seg) :site site :k k :deliver {:deliver :return}}\n      (let [pc (inc site)]\n        {:segment (:address seg) :pc pc\n         :env (canonical-env cx seg pc (:frames entry) (:store-of entry))\n         :window (slice-window cx seg pc (peek parts))\n         :k k\n         :deliver {:deliver :rd :rd (code/rd (inst seg site))}}))))\n\n\n(defn lift-state\n  \"A kernel's wait entry, parked record or reified payload as the\n   canonical act or tail payload (§4.2, §4.3), engine fields carried.\"\n  [cx entry]\n  (let [fields (apply dissoc entry kernel-keys)]\n    (merge (cond-> fields (contains? fields :datom) (update :datom #(canonical-value cx %)))\n           (if (= :stack (:kind cx)) (lift-stack cx entry) (lift-register cx entry)))))\n\n\n(defn lift-context\n  \"The lift context of kernel `k` over `space`; positional closures and\n   kernel continuations are reminted under `owner`.\"\n  [k space owner]\n  (assoc {} :kind (kernel-kind k) :kernel k :space space :free-env (or (:free-env k) {}) :owner owner))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Lower: a canonical act or tail into a kernel\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- lower-frames\n  [lx seg pc env]\n  (mapv (fn [f] (mapv #(positional-value lx %) f)) (frames-of seg pc env)))\n\n\n(defn- payload-segment\n  [lx p]\n  (segment-of (:space lx) (address-of lx (:segment p))))\n\n\n(defn- lower-regs\n  \"`(sort-by first [[phys(v) V] …])` over window `w`.\"\n  [lx seg site w]\n  (vec (sort-by first (map (fn [[x v]] [(phys seg site x) (positional-value lx v)]) w))))\n\n\n(defn- register-k\n  [lx k]\n  (mapv (fn [f]\n          (let [seg (payload-segment lx f)\n                off (offset :register (:kernel lx) seg)\n                pc (:pc f)\n                regs (lower-regs lx seg (dec pc) (:window f))\n                store-of (engine/env-store-of (:env f))]\n            (cond-> {:site-pc (+ off pc -1) :return-pc (+ off pc)\n                     :frames (lower-frames lx seg pc (:env f))\n                     :regs regs :live (mapv first regs)\n                     :dest (phys seg (dec pc) (:rd f))}\n              (some? store-of) (assoc :store-of store-of))))\n        k))\n\n\n(defn- lower-register\n  [lx p fill]\n  (let [k (:kernel lx)\n        seg (payload-segment lx p)\n        off (offset :register k seg)\n        common (cond-> {:segment (:segment k) :format register/format-tag :hash (:hash k)\n                        :image (:register-id seg) :continuation (register-k lx (:k p))}\n                 (< 1 (count (:images k))) (assoc :images (:images k)))]\n    (if (contains? p :site)\n      (cond-> (merge common {:site-pc (+ off (:site p)) :pc (+ off (:site p) 1)\n                             :frames (get fill :frames []) :regs [] :live [] :dest nil\n                             :resume-mode :return-result})\n        (some? (:store-of fill)) (assoc :store-of (:store-of fill)))\n      (let [pc (:pc p)\n            regs (lower-regs lx seg (dec pc) (:window p))\n            store-of (engine/env-store-of (:env p))]\n        (cond-> (merge common {:site-pc (+ off pc -1) :pc (+ off pc)\n                               :frames (lower-frames lx seg pc (:env p))\n                               :regs regs :live (mapv first regs)\n                               :dest (phys seg (dec pc) (get-in p [:deliver :rd]))\n                               :resume-mode :write-result})\n          (some? store-of) (assoc :store-of store-of))))))\n\n\n(defn- layout-slice\n  \"`(mapv W (stack-layout (dec pc)))`, every member present in W.\"\n  [lx seg pc w]\n  (mapv (fn [x]\n          (when-not (contains? w x)\n            (refuse! :yin.k/undecodable :window-missing {:yin.k/pc pc :yin.k/register x}))\n          (positional-value lx (get w x)))\n        (stack-layout seg (dec pc))))\n\n\n(defn- stack-k\n  \"`[frames stack]`: each return frame's slice appended in order, its base\n   the cumulative length through its own slice (§4.3), `b(i) = b(i-1) +\n   |slice(i)|`.\"\n  [lx k]\n  (reduce (fn [[frames st] f]\n            (let [seg (payload-segment lx f)\n                  pc (:pc f)\n                  st (into st (layout-slice lx seg pc (:window f)))\n                  store-of (engine/env-store-of (:env f))]\n              [(conj frames (cond-> {:return-pc (+ (offset :stack (:kernel lx) seg) (a->h seg (dec pc)) 1)\n                                     :frames (lower-frames lx seg pc (:env f))\n                                     :stack-base (count st)}\n                              (some? store-of) (assoc :store-of store-of)))\n               st]))\n          [[] []]\n          k))\n\n\n(defn- lower-stack\n  [lx p fill]\n  (let [k (:kernel lx)\n        seg (payload-segment lx p)\n        off (offset :stack k seg)\n        [frames st] (stack-k lx (:k p))\n        common {:segment (:segment k) :format stack/format-tag :hash (:hash k) :image (:stack-id seg)\n                :continuation frames}]\n    (if (contains? p :site)\n      (cond-> (merge common {:pc (+ off (a->h seg (:site p)) 1) :resume-mode :return-result\n                             :stack st :frames (get fill :frames [])})\n        (some? (:store-of fill)) (assoc :store-of (:store-of fill)))\n      (let [pc (:pc p)\n            store-of (engine/env-store-of (:env p))]\n        (cond-> (merge common {:pc (+ off (a->h seg (dec pc)) 1)\n                               :frames (lower-frames lx seg pc (:env p))\n                               :stack (into st (layout-slice lx seg pc (:window p)))})\n          (some? store-of) (assoc :store-of store-of))))))\n\n\n(def ^:private canonical-keys\n  #{:segment :pc :site :env :window :k :deliver :type :id})\n\n\n(defn lower-state\n  \"Canonical act or tail payload `p` as the receiving kernel's entry\n   (§4.2, §4.3), engine fields carried. `fill` gives a lowered tail's\n   `:frames`/`:store-of` (default `[]`/nil), which the return transition\n   replaces unread (§5.6 item 8).\"\n  ([lx p] (lower-state lx p {}))\n  ([lx p fill]\n   (let [fields (apply dissoc p canonical-keys)]\n     (merge (cond-> fields (contains? fields :datom) (update :datom #(positional-value lx %)))\n            (if (= :stack (:kind lx)) (lower-stack lx p fill) (lower-register lx p fill))))))\n\n\n(defn lower-context\n  \"The lower context into kernel `k` over `space`; `address` maps a\n   payload's or closure's `:segment` to A (default: it is A).\"\n  ([k space] (lower-context k space identity))\n  ([k space address]\n   (assoc {} :kind (kernel-kind k) :kernel k :space space :free-env (or (:free-env k) {})\n          :owner (:owner k) :address address)))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Tasks\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- holds-procedure?\n  \"Whether kernel value `x` is or holds, through guest collections, a\n   closure or continuation.\"\n  [x]\n  (cond\n    (or (values/closure? x) (values/continuation? x)) true\n    (values/host-typed? x) false\n    (map? x) (boolean (some holds-procedure? (concat (keys x) (vals x))))\n    (coll? x) (boolean (some holds-procedure? x))\n    :else false))\n\n\n(defn canonical-task\n  \"Quiescent kernel `k` presented as semantic-register machine `template`\n   (a fresh machine of the same composition) for `rows/lift-task`: code\n   by A from `space`, every wait, parked record and value reconstructed\n   through the layout; resources, stores and counters carried. A running\n   kernel is `:yin.k/not-at-safepoint`; install children are not carried\n   by this phase's layouts; a closure or continuation in the free\n   environment has no finite canonical form (§6.3).\"\n  [k space template]\n  (when (engine/active-continuation? k)\n    (refuse! :yin.k/not-at-safepoint nil {:yin.k/pc (:pc k)}))\n  (when (seq (:installs k))\n    (refuse! :yin.k/unsupported :installs {:yin.k/names (vec (keys (:installs k)))}))\n  (when-let [sym (some (fn [[sym x]] (when (holds-procedure? x) sym)) (sort-by (comp str key) (:free-env k)))]\n    (refuse! :yin.k/non-portable :free-env-value {:yin.k/key sym}))\n  (let [cx (lift-context k space (:owner template))\n        conv #(canonical-value cx %)\n        parked (into {} (map (fn [[id rec]] [id (assoc (lift-state cx rec) :type :parked-continuation :id id)]))\n                     (:parked k))\n        value (:value k)\n        parked-value? (and (map? value) (= :parked-continuation (:type value)) (contains? parked (:id value)))\n        code (into {} (map (fn [[a s]] [a (assoc {} :vector (:vector s) :address a :analysis (:analysis s))]))\n                   (:segments space))]\n    (assoc template\n           :code code\n           :code-aliases (into {} (map (fn [a] [a a])) (keys code))\n           :program nil :control nil :window {} :k nil\n           :resources (:resources k)\n           :capability-secret (:capability-secret k)\n           :free-env (:free-env k)\n           :env (or (:free-env k) {})\n           :store (conv (:store k))\n           :module-stores (conv (or (:module-stores k) {}))\n           :parked parked\n           :wait-set (mapv #(lift-state cx %) (:wait-set k))\n           :ready-queue (:ready-queue k)\n           :value (if parked-value? (get parked (:id value)) (conv value))\n           :id-counter (:id-counter k)\n           :installs {}\n           :halted? (:halted? k)\n           :blocked? (:blocked? k))))\n\n\n(defn lift-task\n  \"§7.1 for a de Bruijn kernel: `rows/lift-task` over its canonical\n   presentation. `template` is a fresh semantic-register machine of the\n   kernel's composition; opts as rows/lift-task's.\"\n  [k space template serve! opts]\n  (rows/lift-task (canonical-task k space template) serve! opts))\n\n\n(defn attach-space\n  \"Kernel `k` holding the derived image of every segment of `space`, in\n   A order (§7.2: derive and attach the image for each A).\"\n  [k space]\n  (let [kind (kernel-kind k)]\n    (reduce (fn [k a]\n              (let [seg (segment-of space a)]\n                (if (= :stack kind)\n                  (stack/attach-image k (:stack seg) vm/stack-contract)\n                  (register/attach-image k (:register seg) vm/register-contract))))\n            k\n            (sort-by str (keys (:segments space))))))\n\n\n(defn machine-space\n  \"The space of the A vectors semantic-register machine `m` holds, and\n   the map from its segment ids to A.\"\n  [m]\n  [(space (map :vector (vals (:code m))))\n   (fn [seg] (or (get-in m [:code seg :address]) (when (contains? (:code-aliases m) seg) seg)))])\n\n\n(defn kernel-task\n  \"Step 12 for a de Bruijn receiver: semantic-register machine `m` (what\n   `rows/lower-task` restored) as fresh kernel `k` of the same\n   composition: every image derived and attached, the free environment\n   set, every wait, parked record and value lowered through the layout.\n   Delivers nothing, runs nothing.\"\n  [m k]\n  (let [[sp address] (machine-space m)\n        k (attach-space k sp)\n        lx (lower-context k sp address)\n        conv #(positional-value lx %)\n        parked (into {} (map (fn [[id rec]] [id (assoc (lower-state lx rec) :type :parked-continuation :id id)]))\n                     (:parked m))\n        value (:value m)\n        parked-value? (and (map? value) (= :parked-continuation (:type value)) (contains? parked (:id value)))]\n    (assoc k\n           :resources (:resources m)\n           :free-env (:free-env m)\n           :store (conv (:store m))\n           :module-stores (conv (or (:module-stores m) {}))\n           :parked parked\n           :wait-set (mapv #(lower-state lx %) (:wait-set m))\n           :ready-queue []\n           :value (if parked-value? (get parked (:id value)) (conv value))\n           :id-counter (:id-counter m)\n           :halted? (:halted? m)\n           :blocked? (:blocked? m))))\n\n\n(defn- lexical-names\n  \"The names the chain binds at `pc` of `v`.\"\n  [v pc]\n  (let [bodies (code/body-ranges v)]\n    (loop [b (code/body-index bodies pc) out #{}]\n      (if-let [owner (:owner (nth bodies b))]\n        (recur (code/body-index bodies owner) (into out (nth (nth v owner) 2)))\n        out))))\n\n\n(declare state-prim)\n\n\n(defn- value-prim\n  \"The path to the first `:prim` row carrier value `x` reaches as kernel\n   payload data: through guest collections, a closure's lexical bindings\n   (its positional frames) and a capture's state; or nil.\"\n  [code x path]\n  (when (and (vector? x) (= :row (first x)))\n    (let [n (second x) ss (:slots n)]\n      (case (:kind n)\n        :prim path\n        (:vec :list :set :map) (some (fn [[i y]] (value-prim code y (conj path i))) (map-indexed vector ss))\n        :closure (let [[a entry _ bindings] ss\n                       v (get code a)\n                       owner (when v (some (fn [pc]\n                                             (let [t (nth v pc)]\n                                               (when (and (= :closure (nth t 0)) (= entry (nth t 3))) pc)))\n                                           (range (count v))))\n                       names (if owner (lexical-names v owner) #{})]\n                   (some (fn [[s y]] (when (contains? names s) (value-prim code y (conj path s))))\n                         (partition 2 (:slots bindings))))\n        :reified (state-prim code (first ss) (conj path 0))\n        nil))))\n\n\n(defn- frame-prim\n  \"A frame's window and lexical bindings (§4.4: the free part is the\n   kernel's :free-env, never payload data).\"\n  [code a pc e w path]\n  (let [names (lexical-names (get code a) pc)]\n    (or (some (fn [[r y]] (value-prim code y (conj path :window r))) (partition 2 (:slots w)))\n        (some (fn [[sym y]] (when (contains? names sym) (value-prim code y (conj path :env sym))))\n              (partition 2 (:slots (first (:slots e))))))))\n\n\n(defn- state-prim\n  [code n path]\n  (let [kframes (fn [k]\n                  (some (fn [[i f]]\n                          (let [[a pc e w] (:slots f)]\n                            (frame-prim code a pc e w (conj path :k i))))\n                        (map-indexed vector (:slots k))))\n        [a pc e w k] (:slots n)]\n    (case (:kind n)\n      :act (or (frame-prim code a pc e w path) (kframes k))\n      :tail (kframes e)\n      nil)))\n\n\n(defn- row-procedure\n  \"The path to the first closure or continuation row carrier value `x`\n   holds, through guest collections; or nil.\"\n  [x path]\n  (when (and (vector? x) (= :row (first x)))\n    (let [n (second x)]\n      (case (:kind n)\n        (:closure :reified) path\n        (:vec :list :set :map) (some (fn [[i y]] (row-procedure y (conj path i))) (map-indexed vector (:slots n)))\n        nil))))\n\n\n(defn- free-env-procedure\n  \"§6.3: a de Bruijn kernel resolves free names through its one\n   `free-env` while a canonical closure snapshots its `env`, so a closure\n   or continuation held in the free environment has no finite canonical\n   form there. The path `[:free-env sym …]` to the first such value of\n   decoded task `task`, or nil.\"\n  [task]\n  (some (fn [[sym x]] (row-procedure x [:free-env sym]))\n        (partition 2 (:slots (nth (:slots task) 5)))))\n\n\n(defn- image-collision\n  \"§4.1: `[ident #{A …}]` for the first image of kind `kind` two carried A\n   derive, or nil. A de Bruijn kernel attaches one image once, so it\n   cannot hold both segments; no enumeration order selects an A. A\n   vector that derives no image is left to the carrier's own checks.\"\n  [code kind]\n  (let [ident (fn [a v]\n                (try\n                  (if (= :stack kind)\n                    (dcode/image-hash (:image (derive/stack-image v)))\n                    (rcode/register-hash (derive/register-image v)))\n                  (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _ [::underivable a])))\n        by-image (reduce (fn [acc [a v]] (update acc (ident a v) (fnil conj #{}) a)) {} code)]\n    (some (fn [[i as]] (when (< 1 (count as)) [i as])) (sort-by (comp str key) by-image))))\n\n\n(defn lower-defect\n  \"What a kernel of `kind` cannot hold, judged on decoded task `task`\n   before anything is attached: two carried A of one image (§4.1), install\n   children (not carried by this phase's layouts), a closure or\n   continuation in the free environment (§6.3), and for the register\n   kernel a primitive function in the payload data of a wait or parked\n   state (a window, a lexical binding, or reached through them), which\n   its restore refuses as `:continuation-registers` (`vm/machine-data?`).\n   nil when it can.\"\n  [task kind]\n  (let [slots (:slots task)\n        code (nth slots 11)\n        collision (image-collision code kind)\n        free (free-env-procedure task)]\n    (cond\n      collision\n      (assoc {} :yin.k/status :yin.k/unsupported :yin.k/kind :ambiguous-image\n             :yin.k/image (first collision) :yin.k/segments (second collision))\n\n      (seq (nth slots 12))\n      (assoc {} :yin.k/status :yin.k/unsupported :yin.k/kind :installs)\n\n      free\n      (assoc {} :yin.k/status :yin.k/unsupported :yin.k/kind :free-env-value :yin.k/path free)\n\n      (= :register kind)\n      (when-let [path (or (some (fn [[i w]] (state-prim code (first (:slots w)) [:frames i]))\n                                (map-indexed vector (nth slots 13)))\n                          (some (fn [[p st]] (state-prim code st [:parked p]))\n                                (partition 2 (:slots (nth slots 8)))))]\n        (assoc {} :yin.k/status :yin.k/unsupported :yin.k/kind :continuation-registers :yin.k/path path))\n\n      :else nil)))\n\n\n(defn lower-task\n  \"§7.2 into a de Bruijn kernel: decode `wire`, refuse what kernel `k`\n   cannot hold (`lower-defect`) before any attach, then `rows/lower-task`\n   into `scratch` (a fresh semantic-register machine of the same\n   composition: the carrier's steps 1-11 and restore) and `kernel-task`\n   into `k`. Throws the first refusal as ex-data.\"\n  ([scratch k wire attach!] (lower-task scratch k wire attach! {}))\n  ([scratch k wire attach! opts]\n   (let [task (rows/decode wire (merge rows/default-budget (:budget opts)))]\n     (when (= :task (:kind task))\n       (when-let [d (lower-defect task (kernel-kind k))]\n         (throw (ex-info \"Layout refused\" d))))\n     (kernel-task (rows/lower-task scratch wire attach! opts) k))))\n","numLines":967,"startLine":1,"totalLines":967}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01HDV7awycPx6oqhfYAcdYGj","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"other"}}]}
