{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CA3Cp5k6yWa5nAcjuxPYzx","type":"tool_result","content":"1619\t### 8.3 Slice 6c: the layouts, the stack seam, the cross-engine lanes\n1620\t\n1621\t**6c-pre, the stack tail-completion seam.** File to change:\n1622\t`src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/stack.cljc` (§4.3): park-entry builders mark a\n1623\ttail-call park `:resume-mode :return-result`; `stack-restore` delivers\n1624\tsuch an entry by the return transition. Test to create:\n1625\t`test/yin/vm/debruijn/stack_tail_completion_test.cljc`: a tail\n1626\teffectful call parked and resumed delivers through `K` (pops the frame,\n1627\ttruncates to its base, pushes the value) and halts with the value when\n1628\t`K` is empty; a tail call in operand position never executes the layout\n1629\tsyntax after it; non-tail parks are unchanged (the old stack tests stay\n1630\tgreen). **Depends on** nothing of 4b or 5.\n1631\t\n1632\t**6c proper.** Files to create: `src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic_register/layout.cljc`\n1633\t(§4); `test/yin/vm/semantic_register/layout_test.cljc`; the two extra\n1634\tlanes added to the 6b harness file. **Depends on:** 5a, 5b (`derive`),\n1635\t6b, 6c-pre.\n1636\t\n1637\t**Acceptance (6c).**\n1638\t\n1639\t1. `layout-test/register-pairing`: for every `P ∈ C`, `phys` is total on\n1640\t   every body's named virtuals; `virt(p, s)` is single-valued at every\n1641\t   reachable boundary pc (§5.6 item 3).\n1642\t2. `layout-test/register-live-is-live-out`: §5.6 item 3's second clause,\n1643\t   tail boundaries `[]`.\n1644\t3. `layout-test/register-rd-from-a`: on `:worked-example`'s register\n1645\t   lane at the inner call's park, the canonical `rd` is `2` while the\n1646\t   kernel's `dest` is `3`; the K frame of a nested non-tail call in\n1647\t   `:depth-3` has its `rd` from A, not its physical `dest`.\n1648\t4. `layout-test/stack-correspondence`: §5.6 item 4.\n1649\t5. `layout-test/stack-layout-is-the-saved-set`: §5.6 item 5 and the\n1650\t   worked cases: `(f (g x) y)` at the inner call → `[1]`; `(f (if c (g)\n1651\t   2) y)` at `(g)` → `[1]`.\n1652\t6. `layout-test/stack-slices-partition`: §5.6 item 9; and the\n1653\t   multi-frame fixture, the expression `(cat [1] ((fn [x] (cat [2] ((fn\n1654\t   [y] (cat [3] (next-of c))) 2))) 1))` under the harness's standard\n1655\t   binding setup: `with-cat` outermost, then `(let1 s (stream/make 4)\n1656\t   (let1 c (cursor-of s) …))` around it (the stream is made inside the\n1657\t   program, as every row does: that is this fixture's chosen setup. A\n1658\t   primitive `cat` supplied in the free environment would sit in a live\n1659\t   slot and is no carrier value, `:continuation-registers`,\n1660\t   `debruijn_register_effects.cljc:196`; an authentic cursor reference is\n1661\t   machine data with an explicit carrier marker, `engine.cljc:899-905`, so\n1662\t   in-program construction of `c` is a fixture choice, not a carrier\n1663\t   restriction). **Derivation of the expression\n1664\t   alone** (`cat` and `c` taken as given): the outer application of\n1665\t   `(fn [x] …)` pops its closure and `1`, leaving the outer `cat` and\n1666\t   `[1]` pushed, so its frame's base is `2`; the inner application leaves\n1667\t   the middle `cat` and `[2]` as well, base `4`; the current activation\n1668\t   has pushed its `cat` and `[3]` and the read has popped its cursor\n1669\t   operand (`stack.cljc:839`), so the operand stack has six values:\n1670\t   slices `[0,2)` = `[cat [1]]`, `[2,4)` = `[cat [2]]`, current `[4,6)` =\n1671\t   `[cat [3]]`, each slice's `stack-layout` being `[operator-rd\n1672\t   literal-rd]` of its `cat` call and equal to that activation's saved\n1673\t   window. **As run**, the three binding applications each pop their\n1674\t   closure and single operand off an otherwise empty stack, so `K` has\n1675\t   **five** frames with bases `0, 0, 0, 2, 4`, slices `[0,0) [0,0) [0,0)\n1676\t   [0,2) [2,4)`, current `[4,6)`, stack length six; the test pins these\n1677\t   bases from the kernel's state, checks the partition, and checks that\n1678\t   lowering the lifted frame emits the same five bases (§4.3; the\n1679\t   before-slice rule would emit `0, 0, 0, 0, 2`).\n1680\t7. `layout-test/env-reconstruction`: §5.6 item 6.\n1681\t8. `layout-test/closures-round-trip`: §5.6 item 7.\n1682\t9. `layout-test/tail-lowering-is-unobservable`: §5.6 item 8.\n1683\t10. `harness/cross-engine-canonical-equality`: law 4 for every row ×\n1684\t    segment under `canonical-under`.\n1685\t11. `harness/cross-engine-lowering`: law 5, six ordered pairs.\n1686\t12. `harness/layout-refusals`: `:yin.k/not-at-safepoint` from a kernel\n1687\t    stepped to a non-safepoint pc; a register entry whose `live` was\n1688\t    tampered reconstructs a frame the validator refuses (`:window-extra`\n1689\t    or `:window-missing` by the tamper's direction).\n1690\t13. kondo clean; `bb test:sub yin.vm` green on three hosts.\n1691\t\n1692\t### 8.4 Phase 7's entry conditions\n1693\t\n1694\t**DECIDED** (frozen §10 phase 7). 6a-6c green on three hosts; the row\n1695\tcarrier the only writer and reader the semantic-register kernel has; a\n1696\tdocumented seam for the holder, checkpoint, ledger and authority paths\n1697\t(phase 7 wires it; phase 6 edits none of them); the Stage D/E scenarios\n1698\t(`stage_e_scenarios.cljc`, `checkpoint_fixtures.cljc`) listed with, for\n1699\teach, the §5.2 row that exercises its parking shape; the export-recovery\n1700\tobject (UCF §7.7.4, format version 1 over the old codec) re-based on the\n1701\trow carrier by phase 7, since it embeds a body; and the free-environment\n1702\tretention seam (§6.3) either landed by the 4b track or the explicit\n1703\t`:free-env` argument threaded through the holder's export path.\n1704\t\n1705\t### 8.5 Ordering and concurrency\n1706\t\n1707\t| | needs | concurrent with |\n1708\t|---|---|---|\n1709\t| 6a | 4b stage 1 (branch) | 4b stage 2, 5a-5c, 6c-pre |\n1710\t| 6c-pre | nothing of 4b or 5 | everything |\n1711\t| 6b | 4b stage 2; 5c (scanners) | 5a, 5b, 6c-pre |\n1712\t| 6c | 5a, 5b, 6b, 6c-pre | 5c |\n1713\t\n1714\tNo file of 4b or phase 5 is edited. The old kernel file\n1715\t`debruijn/stack.cljc` is edited by 6c-pre only, for the seam; the\n1716\tregister kernel is not edited. `handoff.cljc` and the old harness are\n1717\tnot edited.\n1718\t\n1719\t---\n1720\t\n1721\t## 9. Verification honesty\n1722\t\n1723\t- **Hand-derived numbers.** `saved(4, 2) = {1}` and `L(5)` on the worked\n1724\t  example are the phase-3 tests' (`analysis_test.cljc:131-139`). The\n1725\t  stack slices `[f]` at the inner call of `(f (g x) y)` and at `(g)` in\n1726\t  `(f (if c (g) 2) y)` were derived twice from the §4.3 walk and agreed\n1727\t  with the reviewer's derivation; the register `phys(1) = 0`, `phys(2) =\n1728\t  3` follow from phase-5 §6.3 row 2, whose pinned `live` at pc 3 is `[0]`\n1729\t  (`{T0,T3}` minus the destination `T3`), the same set §4.2 step 4 and\n1730\t  §5.6 item 3 compute by subtracting the virtual `rd 2` before mapping.\n1731\t  The multi-frame bases in 6c item 6 (`2, 4` for the expression alone;\n1732\t  `0, 0, 0, 2, 4` as run under the harness's bindings) were derived\n1733\t  twice from the kernel's call arm (`stack.cljc:716-733`, base = height\n1734\t  after popping callee and operands); the first pass forgot the pushed\n1735\t  operator, and revision 2's lowering rule used the height **before**\n1736\t  each slice, which the round-2 review caught and §4.3 now states as\n1737\t  cumulative through the slice. Nothing was run.\n1738\t- **Claims that are checks, not theorems**: the stack operand slice\n1739\t  equals the saved set at non-tail safepoints (§5.6 item 5); the non-push\n1740\t  H ↔ A correspondence (item 4); `virt` single-valued at reachable\n1741\t  boundaries (item 3); layout `E` = evaluator `E` (item 6); the tail\n1742\t  lowering's unused fields are unobservable (item 8); the slices\n1743\t  partition the stack (item 9).\n1744\t- **What is not claimed**: that kernel state round-trips (shadowed outer\n1745\t  positional values are nil-filled; the law is on canonical frames);\n1746\t  that every kernel reconstructs canonical frames (two are named; the\n1747\t  walker is excluded); that today's stack kernel delivers a tail effect\n1748\t  through `K` (it does not; 6c-pre adds it).\n1749\t- **Private access.** Every function a test names is public; no `#'`.\n1750\t- **Unverified.** 4b stage 2 is not landed: rows 3-4, 7-12, 17, 24 are\n1751\t  written against the evaluator design's §1.4-1.6 shapes and the stage-1\n1752\t  branch and must be re-read when stage 2 lands. The seam of §4.3 is a\n1753\t  specification of a change to `stack.cljc`, not a reading of code that\n1754\t  exists. **Amended after 6b (2026-10-13):** 4b stage 2 landed before\n1755\t  6b, and rows 3-4, 7-12, 17 and 24 now run on the reference lane (89\n1756\t  labelled row × segment executions, 85 distinct builder/wrapper setups\n1757\t  since rows 3 and 24 share one builder by design); rows 10-11 were\n1758\t  re-read and corrected (§5.2, B1). The 6b harness ran on the JVM only;\n1759\t  Node and Dart execution of `rows.cljc`'s transport and the new harness\n1760\t  file remain the three-host gate of §8.2 item 9, not established by the\n1761\t  reviews.\n1762\t\n1763\t---\n1764\t\n1765\t## 10. Findings and proposed amendments\n1766\t\n1767\tReviewer rulings (codex gpt-6.1-sol, 2026-10-10): F1, F4, U2, U4, U5,\n1768\tR1, R2, R7, C1 **ACCEPT**; F2, F3, U1, U3, U6, R3, R4, R5, R6, R8, R9"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"47508f4a-f118-4fad-b5f9-49922c52f330","uuid":"bdf19210-42b4-47b9-b01f-44be23b5ab4c","timestamp":"2026-10-13T08:29:53.107Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-docs-6c/docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md","content":"### 8.3 Slice 6c: the layouts, the stack seam, the cross-engine lanes\n\n**6c-pre, the stack tail-completion seam.** File to change:\n`src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn/stack.cljc` (§4.3): park-entry builders mark a\ntail-call park `:resume-mode :return-result`; `stack-restore` delivers\nsuch an entry by the return transition. Test to create:\n`test/yin/vm/debruijn/stack_tail_completion_test.cljc`: a tail\neffectful call parked and resumed delivers through `K` (pops the frame,\ntruncates to its base, pushes the value) and halts with the value when\n`K` is empty; a tail call in operand position never executes the layout\nsyntax after it; non-tail parks are unchanged (the old stack tests stay\ngreen). **Depends on** nothing of 4b or 5.\n\n**6c proper.** Files to create: `src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic_register/layout.cljc`\n(§4); `test/yin/vm/semantic_register/layout_test.cljc`; the two extra\nlanes added to the 6b harness file. **Depends on:** 5a, 5b (`derive`),\n6b, 6c-pre.\n\n**Acceptance (6c).**\n\n1. `layout-test/register-pairing`: for every `P ∈ C`, `phys` is total on\n   every body's named virtuals; `virt(p, s)` is single-valued at every\n   reachable boundary pc (§5.6 item 3).\n2. `layout-test/register-live-is-live-out`: §5.6 item 3's second clause,\n   tail boundaries `[]`.\n3. `layout-test/register-rd-from-a`: on `:worked-example`'s register\n   lane at the inner call's park, the canonical `rd` is `2` while the\n   kernel's `dest` is `3`; the K frame of a nested non-tail call in\n   `:depth-3` has its `rd` from A, not its physical `dest`.\n4. `layout-test/stack-correspondence`: §5.6 item 4.\n5. `layout-test/stack-layout-is-the-saved-set`: §5.6 item 5 and the\n   worked cases: `(f (g x) y)` at the inner call → `[1]`; `(f (if c (g)\n   2) y)` at `(g)` → `[1]`.\n6. `layout-test/stack-slices-partition`: §5.6 item 9; and the\n   multi-frame fixture, the expression `(cat [1] ((fn [x] (cat [2] ((fn\n   [y] (cat [3] (next-of c))) 2))) 1))` under the harness's standard\n   binding setup: `with-cat` outermost, then `(let1 s (stream/make 4)\n   (let1 c (cursor-of s) …))` around it (the stream is made inside the\n   program, as every row does: that is this fixture's chosen setup. A\n   primitive `cat` supplied in the free environment would sit in a live\n   slot and is no carrier value, `:continuation-registers`,\n   `debruijn_register_effects.cljc:196`; an authentic cursor reference is\n   machine data with an explicit carrier marker, `engine.cljc:899-905`, so\n   in-program construction of `c` is a fixture choice, not a carrier\n   restriction). **Derivation of the expression\n   alone** (`cat` and `c` taken as given): the outer application of\n   `(fn [x] …)` pops its closure and `1`, leaving the outer `cat` and\n   `[1]` pushed, so its frame's base is `2`; the inner application leaves\n   the middle `cat` and `[2]` as well, base `4`; the current activation\n   has pushed its `cat` and `[3]` and the read has popped its cursor\n   operand (`stack.cljc:839`), so the operand stack has six values:\n   slices `[0,2)` = `[cat [1]]`, `[2,4)` = `[cat [2]]`, current `[4,6)` =\n   `[cat [3]]`, each slice's `stack-layout` being `[operator-rd\n   literal-rd]` of its `cat` call and equal to that activation's saved\n   window. **As run**, the three binding applications each pop their\n   closure and single operand off an otherwise empty stack, so `K` has\n   **five** frames with bases `0, 0, 0, 2, 4`, slices `[0,0) [0,0) [0,0)\n   [0,2) [2,4)`, current `[4,6)`, stack length six; the test pins these\n   bases from the kernel's state, checks the partition, and checks that\n   lowering the lifted frame emits the same five bases (§4.3; the\n   before-slice rule would emit `0, 0, 0, 0, 2`).\n7. `layout-test/env-reconstruction`: §5.6 item 6.\n8. `layout-test/closures-round-trip`: §5.6 item 7.\n9. `layout-test/tail-lowering-is-unobservable`: §5.6 item 8.\n10. `harness/cross-engine-canonical-equality`: law 4 for every row ×\n    segment under `canonical-under`.\n11. `harness/cross-engine-lowering`: law 5, six ordered pairs.\n12. `harness/layout-refusals`: `:yin.k/not-at-safepoint` from a kernel\n    stepped to a non-safepoint pc; a register entry whose `live` was\n    tampered reconstructs a frame the validator refuses (`:window-extra`\n    or `:window-missing` by the tamper's direction).\n13. kondo clean; `bb test:sub yin.vm` green on three hosts.\n\n### 8.4 Phase 7's entry conditions\n\n**DECIDED** (frozen §10 phase 7). 6a-6c green on three hosts; the row\ncarrier the only writer and reader the semantic-register kernel has; a\ndocumented seam for the holder, checkpoint, ledger and authority paths\n(phase 7 wires it; phase 6 edits none of them); the Stage D/E scenarios\n(`stage_e_scenarios.cljc`, `checkpoint_fixtures.cljc`) listed with, for\neach, the §5.2 row that exercises its parking shape; the export-recovery\nobject (UCF §7.7.4, format version 1 over the old codec) re-based on the\nrow carrier by phase 7, since it embeds a body; and the free-environment\nretention seam (§6.3) either landed by the 4b track or the explicit\n`:free-env` argument threaded through the holder's export path.\n\n### 8.5 Ordering and concurrency\n\n| | needs | concurrent with |\n|---|---|---|\n| 6a | 4b stage 1 (branch) | 4b stage 2, 5a-5c, 6c-pre |\n| 6c-pre | nothing of 4b or 5 | everything |\n| 6b | 4b stage 2; 5c (scanners) | 5a, 5b, 6c-pre |\n| 6c | 5a, 5b, 6b, 6c-pre | 5c |\n\nNo file of 4b or phase 5 is edited. The old kernel file\n`debruijn/stack.cljc` is edited by 6c-pre only, for the seam; the\nregister kernel is not edited. `handoff.cljc` and the old harness are\nnot edited.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Verification honesty\n\n- **Hand-derived numbers.** `saved(4, 2) = {1}` and `L(5)` on the worked\n  example are the phase-3 tests' (`analysis_test.cljc:131-139`). The\n  stack slices `[f]` at the inner call of `(f (g x) y)` and at `(g)` in\n  `(f (if c (g) 2) y)` were derived twice from the §4.3 walk and agreed\n  with the reviewer's derivation; the register `phys(1) = 0`, `phys(2) =\n  3` follow from phase-5 §6.3 row 2, whose pinned `live` at pc 3 is `[0]`\n  (`{T0,T3}` minus the destination `T3`), the same set §4.2 step 4 and\n  §5.6 item 3 compute by subtracting the virtual `rd 2` before mapping.\n  The multi-frame bases in 6c item 6 (`2, 4` for the expression alone;\n  `0, 0, 0, 2, 4` as run under the harness's bindings) were derived\n  twice from the kernel's call arm (`stack.cljc:716-733`, base = height\n  after popping callee and operands); the first pass forgot the pushed\n  operator, and revision 2's lowering rule used the height **before**\n  each slice, which the round-2 review caught and §4.3 now states as\n  cumulative through the slice. Nothing was run.\n- **Claims that are checks, not theorems**: the stack operand slice\n  equals the saved set at non-tail safepoints (§5.6 item 5); the non-push\n  H ↔ A correspondence (item 4); `virt` single-valued at reachable\n  boundaries (item 3); layout `E` = evaluator `E` (item 6); the tail\n  lowering's unused fields are unobservable (item 8); the slices\n  partition the stack (item 9).\n- **What is not claimed**: that kernel state round-trips (shadowed outer\n  positional values are nil-filled; the law is on canonical frames);\n  that every kernel reconstructs canonical frames (two are named; the\n  walker is excluded); that today's stack kernel delivers a tail effect\n  through `K` (it does not; 6c-pre adds it).\n- **Private access.** Every function a test names is public; no `#'`.\n- **Unverified.** 4b stage 2 is not landed: rows 3-4, 7-12, 17, 24 are\n  written against the evaluator design's §1.4-1.6 shapes and the stage-1\n  branch and must be re-read when stage 2 lands. The seam of §4.3 is a\n  specification of a change to `stack.cljc`, not a reading of code that\n  exists. **Amended after 6b (2026-10-13):** 4b stage 2 landed before\n  6b, and rows 3-4, 7-12, 17 and 24 now run on the reference lane (89\n  labelled row × segment executions, 85 distinct builder/wrapper setups\n  since rows 3 and 24 share one builder by design); rows 10-11 were\n  re-read and corrected (§5.2, B1). The 6b harness ran on the JVM only;\n  Node and Dart execution of `rows.cljc`'s transport and the new harness\n  file remain the three-host gate of §8.2 item 9, not established by the\n  reviews.\n\n---\n\n## 10. Findings and proposed amendments\n\nReviewer rulings (codex gpt-6.1-sol, 2026-10-10): F1, F4, U2, U4, U5,\nR1, R2, R7, C1 **ACCEPT**; F2, F3, U1, U3, U6, R3, R4, R5, R6, R8, R9","numLines":150,"startLine":1619,"totalLines":2233}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01CA3Cp5k6yWa5nAcjuxPYzx","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
